1
00:02:16,866 --> 00:02:20,805
So you want an alliance against
the Mongols in exchange for Halime?

2
00:02:20,805 --> 00:02:23,605
You forced me into this, Osman Bey.

3
00:02:24,126 --> 00:02:29,805
You caused this trouble by
killing Esenbike and her son.

4
00:02:29,806 --> 00:02:34,485
Whoever put this blame on us, I will find them.

5
00:02:34,486 --> 00:02:40,045
But their fate will be nothing but death.

6
00:02:47,686 --> 00:02:50,925
Didn't you want to come together with my Poena?

7
00:02:50,926 --> 00:02:53,725
Not Poena, Halime!

8
00:02:56,246 --> 00:02:59,925
Even if you made her forget
her name, she is still my Halime.

9
00:02:59,926 --> 00:03:01,765
Yes, that's true.

10
00:03:02,886 --> 00:03:06,005
I made her forget the tent life.

11
00:03:06,566 --> 00:03:12,085
I raised her like a noble
girl in the palaces of Rome.

12
00:03:13,006 --> 00:03:15,485
You took my daughter from my arms by force.

13
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:20,245
And now you come and set
conditions to give her back to me?

14
00:03:24,246 --> 00:03:29,005
This is your only chance to find her.

15
00:03:32,246 --> 00:03:35,645
Either you agree with me, Osman Bey...

16
00:03:36,366 --> 00:03:41,765
...or I'll send Poena to Constantinople
to protect her from Olcaytu.

17
00:04:07,046 --> 00:04:07,925
Aunt!

18
00:04:08,936 --> 00:04:10,485
Your mouth's bleeding!

19
00:04:10,486 --> 00:04:13,445
I'm dying. Poena.

20
00:04:13,686 --> 00:04:17,165
Is she really dying?

21
00:04:22,566 --> 00:04:27,325
The little gazelle kept running.

22
00:04:27,326 --> 00:04:32,125
She went deep into the forest.

23
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:36,045
Then...

24
00:04:36,046 --> 00:04:37,845
...the Jackal.

25
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:44,125
The jackal came to the gazelle...

26
00:04:44,286 --> 00:04:48,845
...did not make a noise, and said...

27
00:04:49,766 --> 00:04:51,965
..."Little gazelle...

28
00:04:52,086 --> 00:04:55,885
Don't wander around here like this."

29
00:04:55,886 --> 00:04:57,245
Father..

30
00:05:14,806 --> 00:05:16,125
Mother...

31
00:05:21,406 --> 00:05:22,645
No.

32
00:05:23,526 --> 00:05:25,725
I cannot stay here any longer.

33
00:05:43,046 --> 00:05:44,925
Open the door!

34
00:05:45,286 --> 00:05:48,765
Mistress Sofia ordered you not to
leave the room until she returns.

35
00:05:53,046 --> 00:05:54,925
Damn it!

36
00:06:03,886 --> 00:06:05,565
Look Sofia.

37
00:06:05,686 --> 00:06:08,285
Look right into our eyes.

38
00:06:08,566 --> 00:06:10,805
You took our child from us once.

39
00:06:10,806 --> 00:06:12,765
But it won't happen again.

40
00:06:12,766 --> 00:06:15,525
I swear, we will not let
you leave this tribe alive.

41
00:06:15,526 --> 00:06:17,645
Then...

42
00:06:19,526 --> 00:06:22,805
...Poena will be breathing far away from you.

43
00:06:28,566 --> 00:06:30,205
Look at me.

44
00:06:30,966 --> 00:06:35,805
Don't you have even a
little bit of honor or grace?

45
00:06:35,806 --> 00:06:37,885
For me, honor...

46
00:06:39,326 --> 00:06:43,765
...means protecting my
land from Turks and Mongols.

47
00:06:44,966 --> 00:06:50,885
And don't forget, you are the invaders.

48
00:06:50,886 --> 00:06:55,645
Your rule only brings cruelty to the people.

49
00:06:55,646 --> 00:06:58,005
The real matter is to help the oppressed.

50
00:06:58,006 --> 00:07:03,045
Then you won't turn your
back on the people of Bursa.

51
00:07:03,046 --> 00:07:05,285
Because of you...

52
00:07:05,406 --> 00:07:07,765
...the Mongols will kill them.

53
00:07:08,646 --> 00:07:12,525
Until we fight against each other again...

54
00:07:13,886 --> 00:07:15,725
...we will get over...

55
00:07:16,526 --> 00:07:20,005
...this trouble together.

56
00:07:22,126 --> 00:07:25,805
Think and decide.

57
00:07:25,806 --> 00:07:29,765
But for the fate of the borders and Poena...

58
00:07:32,286 --> 00:07:34,005
...this is the last chance.

59
00:07:39,286 --> 00:07:41,645
Gather the council now!

60
00:07:42,286 --> 00:07:44,885
Are we going to let her go, my Bey?

61
00:07:57,526 --> 00:07:59,605
Mother, this devil is leaving.

62
00:07:59,766 --> 00:08:02,005
Are we going to let her go?

63
00:08:02,566 --> 00:08:06,605
If we don't make an alliance,
we can't see your sister again.

64
00:08:07,766 --> 00:08:12,725
But we cannot make an alliance with this demon.

65
00:08:42,686 --> 00:08:47,645
She didn't just take my
memories, but my hair too.

66
00:08:48,726 --> 00:08:51,485
I don't look like you, mother.

67
00:09:00,246 --> 00:09:04,765
You are merciful. You are good.

68
00:09:05,686 --> 00:09:07,165
And I...

69
00:09:08,726 --> 00:09:12,085
I betrayed you.

70
00:09:23,926 --> 00:09:25,805
How can I come to you?

71
00:09:25,886 --> 00:09:30,605
How can I look into those beautiful
eyes that shed tears for me?

72
00:09:32,246 --> 00:09:34,205
I can't come, mother.

73
00:09:35,566 --> 00:09:37,245
I can't look at your face.

74
00:09:39,646 --> 00:09:41,725
Forgive me, mother.

75
00:09:44,966 --> 00:09:47,085
Forgive me, father..

76
00:09:49,766 --> 00:09:52,525
In the council of Beys, we set our target.

77
00:09:53,006 --> 00:09:55,605
We lost countless martyrs for this cause.

78
00:09:56,126 --> 00:10:01,605
But snake Sofia's offer of peace
requires us not to claw the headquarters.

79
00:10:02,246 --> 00:10:03,765
Right, my Bey?

80
00:10:04,886 --> 00:10:07,645
They're threatening me...

81
00:10:11,406 --> 00:10:13,605
...with my precious daughter.

82
00:10:17,086 --> 00:10:18,125
But no.

83
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:23,045
I will neither leave my martyrs to heathens...

84
00:10:23,726 --> 00:10:28,485
...or stop before capturing
these lands watered...

85
00:10:30,006 --> 00:10:31,325
...with their blood.

86
00:10:31,766 --> 00:10:33,205
When you give the order.

87
00:10:33,446 --> 00:10:34,885
...we will never avoid...

88
00:10:35,046 --> 00:10:39,965
...taking revenge and capturing that heathen
nest which opens a door into Bursa, my Bey.

89
00:10:43,566 --> 00:10:45,765
What about my sister Halime, my Bey?

90
00:10:45,926 --> 00:10:47,765
When we capture the headquarters.

91
00:10:48,646 --> 00:10:50,525
...Sofia will take her away.

92
00:10:52,766 --> 00:10:54,645
This is such a challenge...

93
00:10:57,046 --> 00:11:00,085
Whichever direction we
go, it will hurt out hearts.

94
00:11:00,126 --> 00:11:02,365
You think it doesn't hurt our hearts...

95
00:11:03,206 --> 00:11:05,325
...while we decide to fight?

96
00:11:06,806 --> 00:11:09,245
We won't leave my sister to heathens.

97
00:11:09,406 --> 00:11:11,885
But we won't give up either...

98
00:11:12,446 --> 00:11:14,645
...by trusting demon Sofia's words.

99
00:11:15,726 --> 00:11:18,965
Those who shout the
requirements of being a Bey...

100
00:11:20,366 --> 00:11:24,165
...also know that a Bey should suspect first.

101
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:27,445
No, not at all.

102
00:11:28,206 --> 00:11:30,845
I can say no words before great Orhan Bey.

103
00:11:31,406 --> 00:11:32,485
Alaaddin.

104
00:11:33,686 --> 00:11:36,765
When did you become so shortsighted?

105
00:11:38,286 --> 00:11:40,565
You're even afraid of the word fight.

106
00:11:40,886 --> 00:11:44,125
You say drawing back to
survive is a shortsighted action.

107
00:11:44,886 --> 00:11:48,845
What about sending your soldiers
to death on purpose for ambition?

108
00:11:50,446 --> 00:11:52,525
You call me shortsighted, but...

109
00:11:53,286 --> 00:11:54,405
...you are improvident.

110
00:11:54,566 --> 00:11:56,845
You think desire to fight is ambition...

111
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,525
..and not giving up is a mistake, huh?

112
00:12:00,046 --> 00:12:01,645
Alaaddin.

113
00:12:02,366 --> 00:12:06,805
I used to see you as a high
mountain that I could lean on.

114
00:12:07,606 --> 00:12:09,435
What a shame, you turned out to be nothing!

115
00:12:09,435 --> 00:12:10,685
-Orhan Bey!
-Enough!

116
00:12:13,166 --> 00:12:14,885
How impudent you two are!

117
00:12:17,646 --> 00:12:19,605
How impertinent you are before me!

118
00:12:25,646 --> 00:12:27,725
What are you doing? Look at me!

119
00:12:29,166 --> 00:12:30,445
Look at me!

120
00:12:32,846 --> 00:12:34,885
Didn't I tell you boys...

121
00:12:35,486 --> 00:12:37,925
...whoever causes unrest has no place beside me?

122
00:12:39,046 --> 00:12:40,645
Answer me!

123
00:12:41,566 --> 00:12:43,325
So let me, my Bey.

124
00:12:45,206 --> 00:12:47,485
Although it breaks my heart apart,

125
00:12:49,206 --> 00:12:51,525
...let me be the one to separate his way.

126
00:12:58,686 --> 00:13:01,525
So our tribe will have peace...

127
00:13:02,886 --> 00:13:06,005
...and the state will have no unrest.

128
00:13:08,206 --> 00:13:09,125
Let me..

129
00:13:10,846 --> 00:13:13,485
Let me be the one to miss his family.

130
00:13:15,406 --> 00:13:18,925
So the one who says he is
always right will be the Bey.

131
00:13:19,726 --> 00:13:21,405
So he can have both the feast...

132
00:13:22,286 --> 00:13:23,765
..and the hunt!

133
00:13:25,766 --> 00:13:26,565
My Bey.

134
00:13:28,166 --> 00:13:30,405
I don't want to serve my state with my sword...

135
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:33,085
...but with my wisdom in the frontiers.

136
00:13:35,686 --> 00:13:37,485
If I have your approval.

137
00:13:41,366 --> 00:13:43,005
Get out of my sight.

138
00:13:46,646 --> 00:13:48,365
Get out of my sight!

139
00:14:02,846 --> 00:14:04,765
Whoever wants to leave...

140
00:14:06,206 --> 00:14:07,645
...must go now!

141
00:14:10,686 --> 00:14:11,645
Come on!

142
00:14:20,646 --> 00:14:22,965
With the rest, we will draw our route.

143
00:14:28,766 --> 00:14:29,605
Gonca.

144
00:14:29,646 --> 00:14:32,445
Make your preparations. We're leaving the tribe.

145
00:14:32,446 --> 00:14:33,845
What are you talking about?

146
00:14:33,966 --> 00:14:35,645
What? Where are you going?

147
00:14:35,846 --> 00:14:38,565
Mother, I can't stay here any longer.

148
00:14:39,286 --> 00:14:42,325
We're going to the dervish
lodge to be with my grandfather.

149
00:14:42,486 --> 00:14:43,565
Why?

150
00:14:45,526 --> 00:14:48,685
Mother, if I stay here,

151
00:14:49,286 --> 00:14:50,765
...there will be unrest.

152
00:14:51,606 --> 00:14:57,285
As long as I'm here, there
will be no peace in this tribe.

153
00:14:58,086 --> 00:14:59,445
So I will retreat.

154
00:15:03,006 --> 00:15:04,765
And nobody else will be hurt.

155
00:15:05,326 --> 00:15:08,525
Alaaddin, my son... What does your father say?

156
00:15:08,646 --> 00:15:10,205
He won't let you go.

157
00:15:10,246 --> 00:15:11,605
You can't go.

158
00:15:12,566 --> 00:15:14,165
My father let me, mother.

159
00:15:14,766 --> 00:15:15,765
What?

160
00:15:17,726 --> 00:15:19,525
And he made his decision.

161
00:15:19,926 --> 00:15:21,765
He won't have a deal with Sofia.

162
00:15:23,126 --> 00:15:26,365
He'll raid the headquarters
and take our martyrs.

163
00:15:27,126 --> 00:15:29,165
He won't have a deal with Sofia?

164
00:15:29,966 --> 00:15:32,005
We won't be able to see Halime then.

165
00:15:33,406 --> 00:15:34,605
Sofia.

166
00:15:37,846 --> 00:15:40,445
She wants an alliance against Mongolians.

167
00:15:41,286 --> 00:15:43,685
We'll see if her intention is good or not.

168
00:15:44,086 --> 00:15:49,525
If she still has the same intention after we
captured the headquarters of Derince tomorrow,

169
00:15:55,326 --> 00:15:56,765
..then..

170
00:15:58,726 --> 00:16:02,165
...we will have a temporary
alliance against Mongolians.

171
00:16:02,766 --> 00:16:06,965
If Sofia changes her mind
about the alliance after this

172
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:10,445
...you may never be able to see your daughter.

173
00:16:17,606 --> 00:16:18,285
Hatun.

174
00:16:18,366 --> 00:16:20,405
Finish your preparations quickly.

175
00:16:20,526 --> 00:16:22,845
We're leaving tomorrow in the morning.

176
00:16:27,366 --> 00:16:28,245
Mother.

177
00:16:28,486 --> 00:16:30,085
What about my sister?

178
00:16:30,926 --> 00:16:33,525
We will never be able to find her.

179
00:16:38,526 --> 00:16:39,605
Bring the horse!

180
00:16:39,766 --> 00:16:41,645
Osman, what are you doing?

181
00:16:42,686 --> 00:16:46,605
Are you sending my son away
and leaving my daughter to her fate?

182
00:16:51,006 --> 00:16:52,285
Osman!

183
00:16:53,246 --> 00:16:54,205
Osman!

184
00:16:54,286 --> 00:16:55,445
Osman Bey!

185
00:16:55,886 --> 00:16:57,245
Bring my horse!

186
00:16:59,006 --> 00:17:00,445
What are you doing, Osman?

187
00:17:00,646 --> 00:17:02,365
We need to talk.

188
00:17:06,606 --> 00:17:07,845
Come on!

189
00:17:11,766 --> 00:17:13,805
Our people are on the way, Koca Bey.

190
00:17:14,965 --> 00:17:17,005
May Allah be pleased with Osman Bey.

191
00:17:17,126 --> 00:17:19,484
He gave us a homeland and protected us.

192
00:17:19,766 --> 00:17:22,685
And he demanded nothing in return.

193
00:17:23,246 --> 00:17:26,085
Osman Bey is not only a Bey.

194
00:17:27,205 --> 00:17:31,925
He's also the inheritor of
the Turkish state's mind.

195
00:17:32,886 --> 00:17:36,205
He knows traditions and morals.

196
00:17:36,966 --> 00:17:39,885
So his door is open to everyone.

197
00:17:40,446 --> 00:17:44,045
As long as the target is the same.

198
00:17:44,606 --> 00:17:46,205
You're right, Koca Bey.

199
00:17:47,246 --> 00:17:54,045
When our people arrive safely,
we will join Osman Bey's path.

200
00:17:54,446 --> 00:17:56,565
With great pleasure.

201
00:18:09,646 --> 00:18:12,925
Those people coming are Koca
Bey's and Hasan Bey's people.

202
00:18:13,046 --> 00:18:15,565
Osman gave them a land to settle in.

203
00:18:18,966 --> 00:18:27,005
Before Osman shapes in flesh and bones.
I'll cut his flesh and bones into pieces!

204
00:18:35,286 --> 00:18:38,245
The news about the raid will drive Osman mad.

205
00:18:39,486 --> 00:18:40,725
Let him be mad.

206
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:45,045
I'll get him enslaved by his anger, Hristo.

207
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:50,445
Kill them.

208
00:18:51,566 --> 00:18:52,965
Kill them all

209
00:19:04,006 --> 00:19:05,485
Osman!

210
00:19:09,566 --> 00:19:11,125
Osman!

211
00:19:13,006 --> 00:19:14,485
Osman!

212
00:19:23,486 --> 00:19:24,725
Osman.

213
00:19:30,246 --> 00:19:32,445
How could you let Alaaddin leave?

214
00:19:32,726 --> 00:19:34,565
How could you approve that?

215
00:19:34,646 --> 00:19:36,605
I didn't approve anything.

216
00:19:38,246 --> 00:19:39,685
He said he would leave.

217
00:19:41,526 --> 00:19:43,085
And I let him.

218
00:19:43,366 --> 00:19:44,845
You told him to go?

219
00:19:45,046 --> 00:19:46,205
Bala.

220
00:19:51,846 --> 00:19:53,605
He said he would leave.

221
00:19:56,446 --> 00:19:58,245
He showed weakness.

222
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:01,805
He's afraid of a power struggle, Osman.

223
00:20:02,046 --> 00:20:04,005
Who would have a power struggle?

224
00:20:06,046 --> 00:20:07,325
They are young.

225
00:20:07,366 --> 00:20:08,805
They made a mistake.

226
00:20:08,806 --> 00:20:10,285
But this can't be punishment.

227
00:20:10,286 --> 00:20:13,325
I'm offering them a glorious state dream.

228
00:20:13,646 --> 00:20:15,205
It's such a dream...

229
00:20:16,526 --> 00:20:18,725
...that there is no place for mistakes.

230
00:20:20,446 --> 00:20:21,485
This path...

231
00:20:24,046 --> 00:20:26,285
...can't be completed with half-hearted ones.

232
00:20:30,966 --> 00:20:32,405
You don't know.

233
00:20:32,806 --> 00:20:34,485
He's not half-hearted.

234
00:20:36,286 --> 00:20:41,365
Leaving in silence shows the wound in his heart.

235
00:20:45,046 --> 00:20:46,925
I'm not only a father.

236
00:20:50,206 --> 00:20:51,885
I'm the head of the state.

237
00:20:53,446 --> 00:20:55,605
I don't care about a son's sorrow...

238
00:20:57,366 --> 00:20:59,285
...but the burden on my nation.

239
00:21:01,606 --> 00:21:05,805
Does the burden of the state
overweights the burden of your son?

240
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:10,925
You didn't hear his silence.

241
00:21:12,446 --> 00:21:14,525
Because your heart was broken too.

242
00:21:14,766 --> 00:21:17,045
So you kept silent because you were hurt.

243
00:21:17,246 --> 00:21:19,525
Thinking that your son disappointed you.

244
00:21:20,966 --> 00:21:24,365
But your silence made us lose a son.

245
00:21:28,006 --> 00:21:29,885
I'm out of words now.

246
00:21:31,846 --> 00:21:33,565
But I have words to say.

247
00:21:39,086 --> 00:21:40,925
Although he's our son,

248
00:21:42,606 --> 00:21:46,725
...this tribe, this nation, this state...

249
00:21:49,206 --> 00:21:51,365
...can never tolerate weakness.

250
00:21:56,286 --> 00:21:57,565
Fine.

251
00:21:57,686 --> 00:22:00,285
Alaaddin said he'd go and you told him to go.

252
00:22:00,366 --> 00:22:02,845
What about Halime? Our daughter?

253
00:22:04,046 --> 00:22:05,565
Why sacrifice her?

254
00:22:05,846 --> 00:22:07,725
You gave up on your son.

255
00:22:09,366 --> 00:22:12,405
I'm asking you this as a
mother who lost her child.

256
00:22:13,326 --> 00:22:15,965
Are you going to turning your back on her too?

257
00:22:17,326 --> 00:22:19,925
How can you leave our daughter, Osman Bey?

258
00:22:20,246 --> 00:22:24,685
What if we take the headquarters and
our martyrs but lose Halime for ever?

259
00:22:28,886 --> 00:22:33,405
You think it was easy to make this decision?

260
00:22:36,406 --> 00:22:38,725
I prayed before sleeping every night.

261
00:22:39,806 --> 00:22:41,405
I remembered my daughter.

262
00:22:43,966 --> 00:22:48,045
But when I woke up...

263
00:22:51,606 --> 00:22:53,685
...I woke up with the burden of my nation.

264
00:22:56,486 --> 00:23:00,685
I'm not a mother to only the state
but also my children, Osman Bey.

265
00:23:01,726 --> 00:23:05,525
You didn't sacrifice only Alaaddin and Halime...

266
00:23:06,046 --> 00:23:07,565
...but also me today.

267
00:23:09,406 --> 00:23:12,205
I accepted walking beside you.

268
00:23:13,206 --> 00:23:15,805
But you left me behind.

269
00:23:17,686 --> 00:23:22,125
As you carried the state's
burden, you ignored your children.

270
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:25,925
Today,

271
00:23:27,766 --> 00:23:30,405
...you broke my heart into
pieces, Osman the Brunette.

272
00:23:37,406 --> 00:23:39,205
This is a state matter.

273
00:23:42,126 --> 00:23:43,485
At times..

274
00:23:45,886 --> 00:23:48,765
...your heart should be broken into pieces.

275
00:24:29,326 --> 00:24:30,885
My Bey...

276
00:24:35,086 --> 00:24:37,245
What happened to you, my valiant?

277
00:24:37,246 --> 00:24:39,365
We were raided, my Koca Bey.

278
00:24:39,566 --> 00:24:41,445
They killed our people.

279
00:24:41,486 --> 00:24:43,965
They even killed children and the elderly.

280
00:24:43,966 --> 00:24:45,685
They killed all of them.

281
00:24:45,686 --> 00:24:47,765
Who made this treacherous plan?

282
00:24:47,766 --> 00:24:50,045
The Byzantium infidels, my Bey.

283
00:24:50,606 --> 00:24:52,165
Help please.

284
00:24:57,486 --> 00:25:03,725
If I don't take my revenge for
this, may they not call me Koca Bey!

285
00:25:07,126 --> 00:25:09,405
Come on! To horses!

286
00:25:09,486 --> 00:25:10,965
Bury our Alp.

287
00:25:10,966 --> 00:25:12,725
As you order my Bey.

288
00:25:18,766 --> 00:25:19,805
Come on!

289
00:26:21,806 --> 00:26:26,805
Help us, my Allah...

290
00:26:29,686 --> 00:26:31,285
My Allah..

291
00:26:38,966 --> 00:26:41,965
My dear, my little child...

292
00:26:42,326 --> 00:26:44,525
They killed our people, Koca Bey.

293
00:26:44,726 --> 00:26:46,885
They killed my mother.

294
00:26:46,886 --> 00:26:49,085
What was our fault?

295
00:26:49,086 --> 00:26:51,565
Why did they do this?

296
00:26:51,926 --> 00:26:56,165
We will surely make
those who did this pay for it.

297
00:26:56,806 --> 00:26:58,445
Surely.

298
00:27:00,006 --> 00:27:00,965
My Bey.

299
00:27:01,526 --> 00:27:03,725
The rest of the people are coming from behind.

300
00:27:03,846 --> 00:27:09,245
We came ahead to reach
you first, but we were attacked.

301
00:27:09,406 --> 00:27:11,605
Who attacked you?

302
00:27:11,606 --> 00:27:13,525
Give me his name...

303
00:27:13,526 --> 00:27:16,605
So I can cut his body into pieces!

304
00:27:39,646 --> 00:27:41,205
Cladius!

305
00:27:41,726 --> 00:27:43,445
Take position!

306
00:27:44,686 --> 00:27:46,205
Archers!

307
00:27:51,286 --> 00:27:54,325
...you were the two-horned devil...

308
00:27:54,326 --> 00:27:57,605
...who killed my innocent people, huh?

309
00:27:57,606 --> 00:27:59,845
If I am in a war.

310
00:27:59,846 --> 00:28:01,845
...then I don't..

311
00:28:02,526 --> 00:28:05,605
...care if it's children women, or men.

312
00:28:05,606 --> 00:28:08,125
I kill whoever crosses my path.

313
00:28:08,286 --> 00:28:11,405
Come down here if you have some courage!

314
00:28:11,406 --> 00:28:14,205
Don't hide behind your soldiers!

315
00:28:23,886 --> 00:28:26,245
My sword does not come out of its sheath.

316
00:28:26,246 --> 00:28:27,965
I wonder why...

317
00:28:30,966 --> 00:28:32,725
It says...

318
00:28:32,726 --> 00:28:36,245
...it won't deal with old men like you.

319
00:28:36,566 --> 00:28:38,085
And it is right.

320
00:28:39,286 --> 00:28:40,605
Besides...

321
00:28:40,606 --> 00:28:42,885
...I don't want to kill you.

322
00:28:43,126 --> 00:28:44,485
Why?

323
00:28:47,046 --> 00:28:48,645
Because...

324
00:28:48,646 --> 00:28:51,485
...you will convey my greetings to Osman Bey.

325
00:28:51,766 --> 00:28:54,085
Say whatever you want, infidel!

326
00:28:54,086 --> 00:28:55,685
Stop playing games!

327
00:28:55,686 --> 00:28:58,005
Go and tell Osman what happened here.

328
00:28:58,006 --> 00:28:59,165
Tell him that..

329
00:28:59,446 --> 00:29:02,485
...Cladius will be waiting
for him at the outpost.

330
00:29:03,766 --> 00:29:05,725
If you want to die as well...

331
00:29:05,726 --> 00:29:08,245
...if you are bored of living...

332
00:29:08,246 --> 00:29:10,005
...I will be waiting for you as well.

333
00:29:10,366 --> 00:29:12,405
Hristo

334
00:29:27,166 --> 00:29:29,405
Let's go after them my Bey!

335
00:29:30,046 --> 00:29:31,925
We won't.

336
00:29:32,086 --> 00:29:36,350
Since they dared to come
all the way here and face us...

337
00:29:36,362 --> 00:29:40,805
...they won't retreat without
an ambush behind them.

338
00:29:41,206 --> 00:29:44,085
He called us to the outpost on purpose.

339
00:29:44,126 --> 00:29:46,725
It's clear that the game he set up is big.

340
00:29:46,806 --> 00:29:49,885
Let's go and inform Osman Bey, Koca Bey.

341
00:29:50,006 --> 00:29:52,045
Even if he waits for us...

342
00:29:52,046 --> 00:29:56,005
...we will destroy that outpost, Hasan Bey.

343
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:09,165
Alaeddin

344
00:30:10,246 --> 00:30:13,325
My Allah, give me patience.

345
00:30:15,486 --> 00:30:17,805
What do you think you are doing, Alaeddin?

346
00:30:17,806 --> 00:30:20,325
How can you leave the tribe?

347
00:30:21,566 --> 00:30:23,485
I don't have to answer you.

348
00:30:23,486 --> 00:30:25,285
Don't stand in my way.

349
00:30:25,286 --> 00:30:27,045
Alaeddin...

350
00:30:28,526 --> 00:30:31,005
You made a mistake at that outpost.

351
00:30:31,166 --> 00:30:33,485
And you are on the wrong way again.

352
00:30:34,926 --> 00:30:36,805
While you still have time..

353
00:30:38,006 --> 00:30:40,005
...give up on this path.

354
00:30:40,126 --> 00:30:43,485
There is no right or wrong now, Orhan Bey.

355
00:30:44,246 --> 00:30:46,525
The things you told me...

356
00:30:49,166 --> 00:30:51,005
...that punch you threw at me...

357
00:30:52,846 --> 00:30:57,085
I don't want to hear a single
word I don't deserve anymore.

358
00:31:00,326 --> 00:31:04,365
One of us needs to leave
for the peace in our tribe.

359
00:31:04,366 --> 00:31:05,765
And since..

360
00:31:05,766 --> 00:31:07,325
...you have this ambition and...

361
00:31:07,326 --> 00:31:08,665
..arrogance..

362
00:31:10,055 --> 00:31:12,335
...I was going to be the one
who would leave anyway.

363
00:31:12,335 --> 00:31:14,365
Why do you keep talking about arrogance?

364
00:31:14,366 --> 00:31:17,045
We will get in a war soon, Alaeddin.

365
00:31:17,046 --> 00:31:20,565
When we needed even a single man...

366
00:31:20,566 --> 00:31:23,605
...what you are doing is leaving us halfway.

367
00:31:23,606 --> 00:31:25,605
It's helping infidels gain a victory.

368
00:31:25,606 --> 00:31:26,645
Don't...

369
00:31:26,646 --> 00:31:29,565
No... How would that even happen Orhan Bey?

370
00:31:30,046 --> 00:31:32,805
As long as you are at the head of the Alps...

371
00:31:33,206 --> 00:31:35,845
...victory will surely belong to the Kayi.

372
00:31:35,846 --> 00:31:37,925
Why would you need me here?

373
00:31:42,206 --> 00:31:43,845
Alaeddin.

374
00:31:44,126 --> 00:31:45,805
Enough!

375
00:31:46,646 --> 00:31:48,445
Don't touch me!

376
00:31:50,686 --> 00:31:53,965
I will destroy all your
limits and your boundaries.

377
00:31:57,006 --> 00:31:58,725
In this tribe..

378
00:31:59,846 --> 00:32:02,205
...the battle will be yours from now on.

379
00:32:03,726 --> 00:32:06,445
Did I think you were different, Alaeddin?

380
00:32:08,566 --> 00:32:11,045
Have my eyes only just opened?

381
00:32:13,366 --> 00:32:19,205
Is my brother really a man to turn his back...

382
00:32:19,486 --> 00:32:22,565
...and leave when his tribe
is in this situation, in a war?

383
00:32:26,206 --> 00:32:27,925
Orhan Bey.

384
00:32:29,086 --> 00:32:31,605
The war cannot be won with just a sword.

385
00:32:31,606 --> 00:32:36,725
I will go and spill ink to prevent
the shedding of martyr's blood.

386
00:32:39,246 --> 00:32:42,405
I will continue my fight on my front.

387
00:32:42,686 --> 00:32:45,085
Don't worry.

388
00:32:45,686 --> 00:32:48,005
Well done, Alaeddin.

389
00:32:48,006 --> 00:32:49,805
Good. Do that.

390
00:32:50,126 --> 00:32:56,285
But you should know, if we are short by
one, the enemy will be one more than us.

391
00:32:56,286 --> 00:33:01,245
Tomorrow, in that battle, every drop of
blood that will be shed from your family...

392
00:33:02,206 --> 00:33:05,085
...will also be your responsibility.

393
00:33:05,886 --> 00:33:08,805
Go now. Leave.

394
00:33:08,806 --> 00:33:11,525
May Allah let you go safely God willing.

395
00:33:18,606 --> 00:33:20,685
May Allah be pleased with you

396
00:33:20,966 --> 00:33:22,485
..brother.

397
00:33:34,886 --> 00:33:36,925
Peace be upon you.

398
00:33:50,286 --> 00:33:55,245
The wolf's cubs have fallen
into conflict with each other.

399
00:33:57,046 --> 00:34:00,045
We too have fought with my brothers.

400
00:34:00,166 --> 00:34:02,725
We too have fought with my uncle.

401
00:34:04,766 --> 00:34:06,805
Tell me, father.

402
00:34:06,806 --> 00:34:12,445
Did we make your heart suffer like this?

403
00:34:13,166 --> 00:34:14,685
No.

404
00:34:18,446 --> 00:34:20,165
We argued

405
00:34:20,166 --> 00:34:26,605
But even though we fought, we never...

406
00:34:27,806 --> 00:34:29,725
...never...

407
00:34:31,045 --> 00:34:34,605
...showed disrespect in your presence.

408
00:34:35,525 --> 00:34:36,965
Never.

409
00:34:37,846 --> 00:34:42,125
We never turned our backs and parted ways.

410
00:34:43,806 --> 00:34:45,324
Now..

411
00:34:46,646 --> 00:34:49,205
My two sons have become enemies.

412
00:34:49,606 --> 00:34:54,045
And my daughter has disappeared
in the hands of the enemy.

413
00:34:57,366 --> 00:35:00,165
My Halime...

414
00:35:00,206 --> 00:35:04,685
My rose-scented child who
carries my mother's name.

415
00:35:10,166 --> 00:35:12,045
Tell me, father

416
00:35:14,086 --> 00:35:17,285
Which is harder, the test with children...

417
00:35:21,446 --> 00:35:24,285
...the test with the state?

418
00:35:26,526 --> 00:35:30,485
We sometimes...

419
00:35:32,326 --> 00:35:34,765
..gave up on our children.

420
00:35:34,766 --> 00:35:36,285
But..

421
00:35:37,366 --> 00:35:40,245
...we never gave up on the state.

422
00:35:40,846 --> 00:35:43,925
And we never will.

423
00:36:11,966 --> 00:36:14,325
Did you achieve your goal, brother?

424
00:36:15,326 --> 00:36:18,925
Has the anger inside you disappear?

425
00:36:19,566 --> 00:36:21,605
Enough, Cerkutay.

426
00:36:23,926 --> 00:36:26,365
Everything is clear. Don't you see?

427
00:36:26,486 --> 00:36:28,605
You have no shame left.

428
00:36:28,686 --> 00:36:29,845
Shame?

429
00:36:32,406 --> 00:36:35,925
Shame for you, honour for me, brother.

430
00:36:35,966 --> 00:36:39,245
Though I appreciate you.

431
00:36:40,526 --> 00:36:44,805
I mean it, you destroyed
the unity in the tribe...

432
00:36:44,806 --> 00:36:48,885
...especially during wartime.

433
00:36:50,286 --> 00:36:51,845
Brother!

434
00:36:55,206 --> 00:36:56,725
Look.

435
00:36:57,246 --> 00:37:04,125
Osman Bey gave up his
own daughter for the state.

436
00:37:04,126 --> 00:37:07,285
What did Alaeddin Bey do?
He can't give up on his honour.

437
00:37:07,286 --> 00:37:09,965
He is defeated by his
mistake and he is now leaving.

438
00:37:09,966 --> 00:37:14,285
Did you leave him any other choice?
Did you leave him any other choice?

439
00:37:14,286 --> 00:37:17,325
You disgraced him before those Alps.

440
00:37:17,326 --> 00:37:19,205
Didn't he deserve it?

441
00:37:20,766 --> 00:37:21,445
Look.

442
00:37:21,446 --> 00:37:25,885
Look around you. Mothers, sisters, and people
are waiting for their martyrs, Cerkutay.

443
00:37:25,886 --> 00:37:29,325
Where are they? At the infidels' borders.

444
00:37:30,086 --> 00:37:33,445
Because of whom? Huh, brother?

445
00:37:33,726 --> 00:37:34,765
Martyrs, huh?

446
00:37:35,966 --> 00:37:39,325
We will take them, brother.

447
00:37:39,326 --> 00:37:40,845
And we won't just take them.

448
00:37:40,846 --> 00:37:45,165
We will turn that land where they
became martyrs into our homeland.

449
00:37:45,166 --> 00:37:46,845
We will, huh?

450
00:37:46,846 --> 00:37:51,485
How will I trust my brother
who I have trusted for years...

451
00:37:51,486 --> 00:37:54,365
...again during the time of war?

452
00:38:00,886 --> 00:38:02,325
Boran.

453
00:38:04,246 --> 00:38:06,805
What do you mean?

454
00:38:06,806 --> 00:38:08,285
Cerkutay.

455
00:38:09,686 --> 00:38:13,525
The one who once runs away from
shahada, always runs away from it!

456
00:38:13,566 --> 00:38:16,965
I will make you swallow that word
now! I will make you swallow it!

457
00:38:16,966 --> 00:38:19,645
-Do it, come on!
-I will! -Do it, brother!

458
00:38:19,646 --> 00:38:21,005
Choose your words wisely!

459
00:38:21,006 --> 00:38:24,005
Cerkutay, am I lying brother? Am I?

460
00:38:24,006 --> 00:38:26,005
Beys, pull yourself together.

461
00:38:26,006 --> 00:38:28,765
Boran Bey, Cerkutay Bey.

462
00:38:29,046 --> 00:38:33,005
You are Beys. The people
are watching us. Don't do this.

463
00:38:36,326 --> 00:38:37,845
Don't, brothers.

464
00:38:37,846 --> 00:38:40,725
Osman Bey shouldn't hear this, it will be bad.

465
00:38:40,726 --> 00:38:45,045
Don't brother, don't.

466
00:38:45,886 --> 00:38:49,085
Come on brother.

467
00:39:08,086 --> 00:39:09,525
Peace be upon you.

468
00:39:09,846 --> 00:39:11,565
Peace be upon you too.

469
00:39:13,006 --> 00:39:16,045
What's the matter? What brought you here?

470
00:39:16,846 --> 00:39:18,965
Our convoy got raided, Osman Bey.

471
00:39:19,606 --> 00:39:21,605
The heathen called Claudius...

472
00:39:22,046 --> 00:39:26,085
...slaughtered our people
ncluding the old and children.

473
00:39:26,246 --> 00:39:31,365
He said he's wait for you with all his strength
in that headquarter which is a snake's nest.

474
00:39:32,846 --> 00:39:36,365
Is that so? Alright then.

475
00:39:38,166 --> 00:39:40,285
I'll give him what he wants.

476
00:39:44,646 --> 00:39:45,885
Let's go.

477
00:39:49,646 --> 00:39:51,245
Ertugrul Bey.

478
00:39:51,846 --> 00:39:56,365
O Ertugrul Bey, the glorious leader of ghazis!

479
00:40:00,166 --> 00:40:02,365
May you rest in heaven.

480
00:40:38,246 --> 00:40:40,805
I have important news
from the tribe, Begum Hatun.

481
00:40:43,966 --> 00:40:45,805
What is so important?

482
00:40:45,846 --> 00:40:49,965
Byzantine witch Sofia wants to work
together with Osman against Mongolians.

483
00:40:50,046 --> 00:40:52,845
And she'll give Osman his daughter as guarantee.

484
00:40:54,446 --> 00:40:56,805
Things will get complicated again.

485
00:40:57,766 --> 00:41:00,205
This fight will be great for us, Ural.

486
00:41:01,286 --> 00:41:05,525
I'll take back my tribe from Osman's
shadow which was stolen from me.

487
00:41:07,166 --> 00:41:10,245
Go back to their tribe and
let me know his every step.

488
00:41:10,606 --> 00:41:12,325
As you order, Begum Hatun.

489
00:41:16,326 --> 00:41:18,605
You took my everything from me.

490
00:41:20,246 --> 00:41:23,645
Yusuf became a martyr...

491
00:41:24,486 --> 00:41:26,805
...hating me because of you.

492
00:41:28,566 --> 00:41:30,765
I'll chase you to the end.

493
00:41:34,486 --> 00:41:36,045
Who are you?

494
00:41:37,926 --> 00:41:39,885
Alps, attack!

495
00:42:01,286 --> 00:42:02,645
Who are you?

496
00:42:03,046 --> 00:42:05,285
I don't know who you serve.

497
00:42:06,006 --> 00:42:08,365
But you made a mistake by confronting me.

498
00:42:40,166 --> 00:42:42,925
Alaeddin Bey can't think
straight due to his anger.

499
00:42:42,926 --> 00:42:44,085
He's making a mistake.

500
00:42:44,086 --> 00:42:46,565
-You have to think...
You think it's Alaeddin's anger?

501
00:42:46,566 --> 00:42:49,805
How could you not see
Alaeddin's patience, Holofira?

502
00:42:50,006 --> 00:42:54,005
If Alaeddin were angry,
he would have hit him back.

503
00:42:54,686 --> 00:42:57,485
Gonca, you're blowing the coals.

504
00:42:57,646 --> 00:43:02,125
If I were the one blowing the coals, we
wouldn't be the ones leaving the tribes.

505
00:43:02,286 --> 00:43:03,845
You can feel at ease now.

506
00:43:03,846 --> 00:43:06,085
Your departure will cause a bigger fire.

507
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:09,485
If Alaeddin Bey accepts his mistake...
-Holofira.

508
00:43:09,646 --> 00:43:11,085
You still call it a mistake!

509
00:43:11,126 --> 00:43:12,765
Enough!

510
00:43:13,526 --> 00:43:15,525
Neither of you are helping!

511
00:43:17,566 --> 00:43:19,565
My children made a mistake!

512
00:43:20,166 --> 00:43:22,445
Why are you following their paths?

513
00:43:24,286 --> 00:43:26,445
Are you blinded by your anger, Gonca?

514
00:43:27,206 --> 00:43:28,365
No, mother.

515
00:43:29,086 --> 00:43:30,125
No.

516
00:43:31,006 --> 00:43:34,605
How can you raise a child
in this situation, Holofira?

517
00:43:35,246 --> 00:43:38,525
How can you teach your
children brotherhood and family?

518
00:43:39,646 --> 00:43:41,365
I’m sorry, mother.

519
00:43:42,406 --> 00:43:43,805
A mother...

520
00:43:44,486 --> 00:43:47,685
A mother is the hearth.

521
00:43:51,166 --> 00:43:54,405
A hatun is the home.

522
00:43:56,766 --> 00:43:59,805
Everybody breaks things and we repair.

523
00:44:00,006 --> 00:44:01,725
And what are you doing?

524
00:44:04,206 --> 00:44:06,325
You are breaking everything down!

525
00:44:09,326 --> 00:44:10,325
Look at me.

526
00:44:10,886 --> 00:44:14,325
I, Bala Hatun, won't let his happen.

527
00:44:16,326 --> 00:44:19,285
If I see you two in this situation again

528
00:44:20,646 --> 00:44:24,245
..you both will lose my favor!

529
00:44:24,646 --> 00:44:25,965
Now get out!

530
00:44:33,686 --> 00:44:35,725
My Allah, give me strength.

531
00:44:51,366 --> 00:44:53,765
Give me strength, my Allah.

532
00:44:54,166 --> 00:44:55,965
Give me strength.

533
00:45:09,726 --> 00:45:10,765
Poena.

534
00:45:12,846 --> 00:45:15,805
How could you lock me in?

535
00:45:16,246 --> 00:45:18,365
You're imprisoning me now?

536
00:45:18,806 --> 00:45:21,405
I did everything to protect you, Poena.

537
00:45:21,926 --> 00:45:23,245
Don't be angry.

538
00:45:23,566 --> 00:45:26,045
The door is opened now. This is your home.

539
00:45:26,086 --> 00:45:27,645
You protected me?

540
00:45:29,166 --> 00:45:33,525
This lock wasn't for the enemy but me.

541
00:45:33,846 --> 00:45:35,085
Poena.

542
00:45:36,126 --> 00:45:37,965
This lock imprisoned me.

543
00:45:38,286 --> 00:45:40,645
People can't be locked inside their own home.

544
00:45:41,886 --> 00:45:43,605
Where were you?

545
00:45:44,326 --> 00:45:45,565
Where did you go?

546
00:45:46,446 --> 00:45:48,085
Why did you lock me?

547
00:45:52,246 --> 00:45:54,445
I was with your parents.

548
00:45:56,886 --> 00:45:58,525
What are you talking about?

549
00:46:00,246 --> 00:46:01,765
What are you talking about?

550
00:46:02,806 --> 00:46:05,565
I will help you meet
your family, my little bird.

551
00:46:06,606 --> 00:46:10,125
If they accept my offer, of course.

552
00:46:12,286 --> 00:46:13,845
What do you mean?

553
00:46:14,286 --> 00:46:15,645
What offer?

554
00:46:16,806 --> 00:46:18,685
Who are my family, Sofia?

555
00:46:26,006 --> 00:46:27,165
Sofia?

556
00:46:27,446 --> 00:46:29,165
Yes.

557
00:46:31,606 --> 00:46:32,574
What about aunt?

558
00:46:32,586 --> 00:46:35,525
You expect me to call
you aunt after all your lies?

559
00:46:37,246 --> 00:46:39,085
I haven't forgiven you.

560
00:46:41,926 --> 00:46:43,565
And I never will.

561
00:46:44,446 --> 00:46:45,805
No.

562
00:46:46,446 --> 00:46:48,525
I can't want you to do that.

563
00:46:49,126 --> 00:46:51,485
I want to redeem myself.

564
00:46:52,646 --> 00:46:54,925
Only to make you happy...

565
00:46:55,846 --> 00:46:58,445
..and see my regret, today...

566
00:47:03,126 --> 00:47:06,045
...I visited my biggest enemy.

567
00:47:09,366 --> 00:47:11,805
In the tribe of Osman and Bala.

568
00:47:16,966 --> 00:47:18,325
Osman and Bala?

569
00:47:20,566 --> 00:47:21,845
Did you...

570
00:47:24,526 --> 00:47:28,685
You are the daughter of Osman
and Bala who are my sworn enemy.

571
00:47:34,526 --> 00:47:36,805
You are Halime.

572
00:48:00,686 --> 00:48:03,805
If you are to point your arrow at the eagle.

573
00:48:04,766 --> 00:48:07,365
...you shouldn't aim where it lands...

574
00:48:07,966 --> 00:48:10,765
...but where it's going to fly off.

575
00:48:37,526 --> 00:48:42,645
This is what I expect from all of you!

576
00:48:47,966 --> 00:48:49,485
Get off!

577
00:49:03,446 --> 00:49:04,885
Who are you?

578
00:49:05,606 --> 00:49:07,085
What do you want from me?

579
00:49:07,726 --> 00:49:08,885
Leave her.

580
00:49:11,886 --> 00:49:13,085
Stand up.

581
00:49:18,046 --> 00:49:21,245
I'm the one who is to ask questions, hatun.

582
00:49:23,646 --> 00:49:26,725
Did you have an alliance with Esenbike?

583
00:49:27,566 --> 00:49:29,845
Did you serve her?

584
00:49:30,006 --> 00:49:33,285
-We had the same target.
-You had the same target?

585
00:49:34,486 --> 00:49:36,365
They all died

586
00:49:36,846 --> 00:49:41,125
I'm really wonder how you survived.

587
00:49:41,766 --> 00:49:43,925
I ran away for my life.

588
00:49:44,326 --> 00:49:48,085
Otherwise, I would have
died like Esenbike and Sargun.

589
00:49:49,206 --> 00:49:55,325
Were you there when Osman
killed Esenbike and Sargun?

590
00:49:58,766 --> 00:49:59,845
Motherl

591
00:50:07,766 --> 00:50:09,045
I was there.

592
00:50:10,246 --> 00:50:13,085
Osman killed them both with no mercy.

593
00:50:15,206 --> 00:50:18,725
You say you had an alliance with Esenbike.

594
00:50:18,886 --> 00:50:21,165
Why didn't you stop Osman?

595
00:50:21,246 --> 00:50:22,885
We were outnumbered.

596
00:50:23,086 --> 00:50:24,605
I was on my own.

597
00:50:25,446 --> 00:50:27,885
And I hid out to take revenge from Osman.

598
00:50:29,886 --> 00:50:32,005
Do you have an alliance...

599
00:50:32,246 --> 00:50:36,685
...with the red woman called
Sofia with your thirst for revenge?

600
00:50:39,046 --> 00:50:41,005
It seems you know everything.

601
00:50:42,006 --> 00:50:45,045
Then you must know why we have an alliance.

602
00:50:48,606 --> 00:50:50,325
You can't..

603
00:50:50,766 --> 00:50:56,045
...take revenge from Osman in this condition.

604
00:50:57,006 --> 00:51:00,605
You lost your alps and your tribe got destroyed.

605
00:51:03,886 --> 00:51:06,045
You have only one option.

606
00:51:11,166 --> 00:51:12,725
I will...

607
00:51:13,486 --> 00:51:18,765
...give you a great chance
to take revenge from Osman.

608
00:51:26,086 --> 00:51:27,525
Who are you?

609
00:51:27,886 --> 00:51:29,285
What do you want from me?

610
00:51:29,326 --> 00:51:33,045
I'm the only person...

611
00:51:34,726 --> 00:51:38,085
...can give you your tribe and revenge.

612
00:51:40,526 --> 00:51:42,765
Now tell me, hatun.

613
00:51:44,246 --> 00:51:46,925
Will you serve me?

614
00:51:52,846 --> 00:51:57,045
You raised me as a executioner.

615
00:51:57,846 --> 00:51:58,765
You..

616
00:52:00,166 --> 00:52:04,325
...sent me to kill my own parents.

617
00:52:05,326 --> 00:52:08,485
your both mother and father.

618
00:52:09,086 --> 00:52:10,445
Look at me, Poena.

619
00:52:11,566 --> 00:52:13,165
I'm a victim too.

620
00:52:13,286 --> 00:52:14,285
You are a victim...

621
00:52:14,366 --> 00:52:16,005
I'm the victim!

622
00:52:16,206 --> 00:52:20,205
-I'm the victim of your war!
-Never! Never!

623
00:52:21,406 --> 00:52:23,125
You are my heart.

624
00:52:23,366 --> 00:52:26,485
Only once... Listen to me only once!

625
00:52:26,846 --> 00:52:28,525
Only once!

626
00:52:29,606 --> 00:52:32,405
Look at the life Osman stole from me!

627
00:52:33,326 --> 00:52:34,845
See what I went through!

628
00:52:36,526 --> 00:52:37,965
Understand me!

629
00:52:39,526 --> 00:52:42,365
Osman threw me into hell!

630
00:52:42,446 --> 00:52:44,965
Do you really think...

631
00:52:45,806 --> 00:52:48,365
...I'm the only evil one?

632
00:52:49,646 --> 00:52:51,685
What about the life you stole from me?

633
00:52:53,286 --> 00:52:56,525
Do you know what kind of hell you threw me into?

634
00:52:58,686 --> 00:53:03,605
Why did you visit Osman and Bala then?

635
00:53:03,886 --> 00:53:05,965
Sofia, tell me.

636
00:53:07,566 --> 00:53:09,845
You're going to use me again, aren't you?

637
00:53:09,886 --> 00:53:14,605
No, I don't want anything from you.

638
00:53:15,606 --> 00:53:17,885
I don't want anything!

639
00:53:18,286 --> 00:53:21,685
I couldn't make you happy, right?

640
00:53:21,886 --> 00:53:22,965
Go then.

641
00:53:27,446 --> 00:53:29,965
-You want me to go?
-Go.

642
00:53:32,526 --> 00:53:34,125
Be happy with them.

643
00:53:42,686 --> 00:53:44,565
But you should know this.

644
00:53:45,646 --> 00:53:47,605
You won't be happy with them.

645
00:53:48,646 --> 00:53:50,725
Because you don't know them yet.

646
00:53:54,486 --> 00:53:57,045
You're going to give me
to them in return for what?

647
00:53:58,366 --> 00:53:59,805
Sofia?

648
00:54:06,566 --> 00:54:08,245
Nothing hard.

649
00:54:09,326 --> 00:54:11,645
An alliance against Mongolians.

650
00:54:13,206 --> 00:54:16,045
I offered Osman a helping hand to protect Bursa.

651
00:54:18,286 --> 00:54:20,765
But it was very hard for me. Poena.

652
00:54:24,966 --> 00:54:27,605
I ended the hostility for you.

653
00:54:28,086 --> 00:54:31,805
Let's see if Osman will make the same sacrifice.

654
00:54:43,206 --> 00:54:45,485
The demon called Claudius...

655
00:54:45,726 --> 00:54:49,205
...slaughtered my alps in
front of the headquarter first.

656
00:54:50,326 --> 00:54:53,005
He's also killed many innocent people of Beys...

657
00:54:53,166 --> 00:54:56,645
...including children and women.

658
00:55:00,726 --> 00:55:04,725
In this huge and vast world.

659
00:55:05,166 --> 00:55:09,325
..I've seen many cruel and merciless acts.

660
00:55:10,406 --> 00:55:12,085
I've seen Mongolians.

661
00:55:12,446 --> 00:55:15,725
I've seen many others
coming from the east, but...

662
00:55:16,086 --> 00:55:20,365
...I had never seen such a heartless enemy.

663
00:55:21,126 --> 00:55:23,965
When I take off their heart with my teeth,

664
00:55:24,366 --> 00:55:26,965
...I will see if they are heartless or not.

665
00:55:29,886 --> 00:55:35,245
We will destroy both the
headquarter and the soldiers in it.

666
00:55:36,526 --> 00:55:38,525
What about your child, Osman Bey?

667
00:55:40,966 --> 00:55:45,565
What if attacking the headquarter
separates you from her permanently?

668
00:55:48,206 --> 00:55:49,885
Did you think about that?

669
00:55:54,846 --> 00:55:58,485
Sofia is a mad one. She'll do what she says.

670
00:56:00,726 --> 00:56:02,485
The state..

671
00:56:04,686 --> 00:56:06,965
...will never act without a plan.

672
00:56:10,086 --> 00:56:11,605
Don't be worrying.

673
00:56:13,046 --> 00:56:15,325
I planned every detail.

674
00:56:17,486 --> 00:56:19,365
My child is my personal matter.

675
00:56:19,686 --> 00:56:21,605
But the conquest of the headquarter...

676
00:56:22,686 --> 00:56:26,685
...is for avenging the martyrs
and the welfare of the state.

677
00:56:28,926 --> 00:56:31,085
It's what I say.

678
00:56:36,206 --> 00:56:39,845
Tomorrow, we're going to
conquer the headquarter.

679
00:56:40,846 --> 00:56:43,565
Koca Bey, Hasan Bey.

680
00:56:44,166 --> 00:56:46,965
You'll go there at dark.

681
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:50,165
And infiltrate secretly.

682
00:56:52,526 --> 00:56:55,805
When we stand against them tomorrow.

683
00:56:56,406 --> 00:56:58,965
...you will push them from the back.

684
00:57:03,886 --> 00:57:10,005
And we will take off their filthy souls.

685
00:57:43,926 --> 00:57:47,125
Jij, no.

686
00:57:48,206 --> 00:57:49,845
Jijig galnish...

687
00:57:49,846 --> 00:57:51,765
Jijig gal...

688
00:57:52,086 --> 00:57:54,765
Jijig galnish..

689
00:57:54,766 --> 00:57:56,365
Brother.

690
00:57:56,366 --> 00:57:59,525
Brother, I have tried many meals in this world!

691
00:57:59,606 --> 00:58:01,725
I have tasted many meals...

692
00:58:01,726 --> 00:58:02,965
Many meals but...

693
00:58:02,966 --> 00:58:05,125
I have never eaten something like this.

694
00:58:05,126 --> 00:58:07,165
I have never eaten something like this brother..

695
00:58:07,166 --> 00:58:09,125
What is this? Where do they cook this?

696
00:58:09,126 --> 00:58:12,685
It is the food of the Chechen
valiants of the Caucasus mountains.

697
00:58:13,206 --> 00:58:18,565
Those valiants eat this meal
and fight against the cruel.

698
00:58:18,566 --> 00:58:22,005
-Oh Praise be. 
-Praise be!

699
00:58:22,006 --> 00:58:28,565
Greetings to the valiants who know the
best food and walk on the right path.

700
00:58:28,566 --> 00:58:30,085
Thank you.

701
00:58:30,166 --> 00:58:33,765
Bless your hands and effort brother.

702
00:58:33,766 --> 00:58:35,645
Thank you, Cerkutay Bey.

703
00:58:37,646 --> 00:58:40,085
Brother, thanks to your hands and arms.

704
00:58:40,086 --> 00:58:44,085
This jijig galnish was very delicious but...

705
00:58:44,566 --> 00:58:47,365
...we cannot feel happy anymore.

706
00:58:48,246 --> 00:58:53,245
So many caravans were raided.
People were killed with swords.

707
00:58:56,206 --> 00:59:02,165
On one side this problem, on the other
side, the conflict between Shahzades.

708
00:59:02,166 --> 00:59:05,405
There is no peace or order
left in the tribe, Cerkutay Bey.

709
00:59:06,366 --> 00:59:08,365
Don't worry.

710
00:59:09,766 --> 00:59:12,325
Are Muslims in trouble for the first time?

711
00:59:13,646 --> 00:59:19,765
But if we stay united and together, we
will get through everything for sure.

712
00:59:19,766 --> 00:59:21,525
For sure.

713
00:59:21,526 --> 00:59:23,325
Besides, our Bey is with us.

714
00:59:23,326 --> 00:59:25,125
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

715
00:59:25,126 --> 00:59:27,854
Even if I had a thousand
lives, I would give them all...

716
00:59:27,866 --> 00:59:30,605
...to Osman Bey who
fights for the path of Islam.

717
00:59:31,846 --> 00:59:33,285
His path is the path of The Righteous

718
00:59:33,286 --> 00:59:36,005
Praise be brother.

719
00:59:36,006 --> 00:59:37,245
He is a valiant.

720
00:59:37,246 --> 00:59:42,725
Victories are won thanks
to courageous men like him.

721
00:59:42,726 --> 00:59:46,085
Now let's eat our meal.
Tomorrow is the time for battle.

722
00:59:46,086 --> 00:59:48,765
Come on. In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

723
00:59:48,765 --> 00:59:54,725
A real battle is won by trusting
your brothers, Cerkutay Bey.

724
00:59:54,846 --> 00:59:59,365
But you and Boran Bey parted ways.

725
01:00:04,166 --> 01:00:06,325
Is that so?

726
01:00:16,246 --> 01:00:18,525
Even if we are apart...

727
01:00:20,206 --> 01:00:22,205
..our hearts are one.

728
01:00:22,206 --> 01:00:26,125
And they beat with the love of war.

729
01:00:28,926 --> 01:00:33,685
Also, we do not seek
separation on the battlefield.

730
01:00:33,686 --> 01:00:35,685
Do not worry.

731
01:00:39,126 --> 01:00:40,885
Now go..

732
01:00:42,646 --> 01:00:45,565
Prepare well for tomorrow.

733
01:00:45,566 --> 01:00:48,445
-Okay.
-Okay.

734
01:02:00,206 --> 01:02:03,925
I cannot sleep. I will get
some fresh air if you allow me.

735
01:02:59,406 --> 01:03:02,085
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

736
01:03:09,166 --> 01:03:11,405
Can I come in, my son?

737
01:03:13,686 --> 01:03:15,485
Come in, mother.

738
01:03:28,046 --> 01:03:29,485
My son.

739
01:03:30,006 --> 01:03:31,485
Mother...

740
01:03:32,566 --> 01:03:34,565
My Alaeddin Ali..

741
01:03:34,806 --> 01:03:39,005
The peace of my heart, the answer to my prayer.

742
01:03:41,246 --> 01:03:43,725
You have already started preparing, huh?

743
01:03:44,926 --> 01:03:46,925
You are in a hurry.

744
01:03:49,606 --> 01:03:52,885
The sooner the better, mother.

745
01:03:56,566 --> 01:03:58,965
Can't you think again, my son?

746
01:03:59,086 --> 01:04:02,765
For our home, for me.

747
01:04:03,606 --> 01:04:05,765
My beautiful mother.

748
01:04:06,246 --> 01:04:08,765
My dear mother.

749
01:04:12,406 --> 01:04:14,845
My decision is certain, mother.

750
01:04:26,766 --> 01:04:29,325
Give me your pardon, mother.

751
01:04:32,646 --> 01:04:34,845
You are leaving me helpless here.

752
01:04:34,846 --> 01:04:38,005
Don't mother... Please don't do this.

753
01:04:42,046 --> 01:04:44,085
I will come back.

754
01:04:45,126 --> 01:04:49,925
I will serve my state with my
knowledge and my pen, God willing.

755
01:04:51,806 --> 01:04:53,085
But..

756
01:04:54,246 --> 01:04:57,365
I need to go now, mother.

757
01:04:59,006 --> 01:05:04,365
The day you held that pen for the
first time, I prayed so much for you.

758
01:05:04,806 --> 01:05:09,285
So that your knowledge would
become a light for your path.

759
01:05:09,286 --> 01:05:11,525
Look, you are saying it, mother.

760
01:05:12,326 --> 01:05:15,645
I am now walking on that prayer's path.

761
01:05:20,246 --> 01:05:21,885
Please, mother.

762
01:05:35,766 --> 01:05:38,765
I found out, my Ali.

763
01:05:44,406 --> 01:05:48,405
Don't say anything, mother.
I don't want others to find out.

764
01:05:48,606 --> 01:05:50,205
Especially not my father.

765
01:05:50,326 --> 01:05:54,405
Don't. I do not want to put
this burden on his shoulders.

766
01:05:55,766 --> 01:06:00,045
I came not to say goodbye to
you but to understand you, son.

767
01:06:00,326 --> 01:06:04,245
But now, when my two
children are blind to each other...

768
01:06:04,246 --> 01:06:06,765
Mother...

769
01:06:09,006 --> 01:06:10,285
Mother.

770
01:06:15,006 --> 01:06:18,045
There is such a fire in my heart that...

771
01:06:18,966 --> 01:06:22,605
The fire keeps growing.

772
01:06:23,566 --> 01:06:26,045
I am afraid of hurting everyone...

773
01:06:27,886 --> 01:06:30,565
...if I run out of patience.

774
01:06:33,966 --> 01:06:36,605
Leaving is the best thing now.

775
01:06:37,086 --> 01:06:40,005
I thought I would come
together with my my daughter...

776
01:06:40,006 --> 01:06:43,165
...but now I will long for
two more children, huh?

777
01:06:43,366 --> 01:06:46,445
It will not be like that, mother, it will not.

778
01:06:47,806 --> 01:06:50,005
You will come together with her, mother.

779
01:06:50,566 --> 01:06:52,965
We will come together with our Halime.

780
01:06:54,086 --> 01:06:57,765
But, I know...

781
01:06:59,046 --> 01:07:02,125
My father will never leave her there.

782
01:07:02,366 --> 01:07:05,765
Alaeddin... Alaeddin...

783
01:07:08,206 --> 01:07:12,525
My son.

784
01:07:30,086 --> 01:07:31,805
Come, my Halime.

785
01:08:25,926 --> 01:08:29,165
He knows the infidels are
looking for a chance to attack.

786
01:08:29,286 --> 01:08:32,685
But what is he going to
do? He is going to leave.

787
01:08:32,685 --> 01:08:35,725
Our Alaeddin Bey will hold his pen...

788
01:08:36,206 --> 01:08:37,845
Especially...

789
01:08:39,126 --> 01:08:42,805
...especially when our state
is in such a difficult position.

790
01:08:43,685 --> 01:08:45,564
Alaeddin.

791
01:08:46,126 --> 01:08:47,484
He can go.

792
01:08:48,685 --> 01:08:52,685
Let him open a new page for himself.

793
01:08:55,845 --> 01:08:58,245
Maybe he won't leave if you talk to him, huh?

794
01:08:58,246 --> 01:09:01,085
I said what I had to say to him, Holofira.

795
01:09:01,566 --> 01:09:03,564
But Alaeddin..

796
01:09:04,206 --> 01:09:08,165
Alaeddin already decided to let us down.

797
01:09:08,685 --> 01:09:10,805
So his cause...

798
01:09:12,645 --> 01:09:15,604
...and his brotherhood were not that strong.

799
01:09:17,046 --> 01:09:18,484
Orhan.

800
01:09:22,126 --> 01:09:24,484
Gonca told me something.

801
01:09:26,886 --> 01:09:30,005
Did you really hit Alaeddin?

802
01:09:33,845 --> 01:09:37,165
Did you tell him to return to madrasa?

803
01:09:47,645 --> 01:09:49,845
Can I come in, my son?

804
01:09:52,046 --> 01:09:53,925
Come in, mother.

805
01:09:59,206 --> 01:10:00,485
My son.

806
01:10:00,486 --> 01:10:01,845
Mother.

807
01:10:02,206 --> 01:10:03,725
My Orhan.

808
01:10:05,486 --> 01:10:07,565
Time passes so quickly, right?

809
01:10:07,566 --> 01:10:09,445
It feels like yesterday.

810
01:10:09,566 --> 01:10:13,725
You and Alaeddin would run and lie on my knees.

811
01:10:14,406 --> 01:10:17,085
I used to tell you about the Messenger of Allah.

812
01:10:17,326 --> 01:10:19,165
-Do you remember, my son? -Mother..

813
01:10:21,246 --> 01:10:25,605
Do you think this situation does not hurt me?

814
01:10:25,606 --> 01:10:28,685
I asked if you remember, Orhan.

815
01:10:29,606 --> 01:10:31,685
I told you that..

816
01:10:32,486 --> 01:10:35,725
...The Messenger of Allah
told his people that...

817
01:10:35,766 --> 01:10:41,085
"The real warrior is the
one who defeats his anger."

818
01:10:43,126 --> 01:10:44,285
Huh, my son?

819
01:10:47,446 --> 01:10:49,205
I remember, mother.

820
01:10:50,406 --> 01:10:52,845
You both were upset.

821
01:10:52,966 --> 01:10:54,845
"How are we going to do that, mother?"

822
01:10:54,846 --> 01:10:57,245
"'Anger is something we can't see...

823
01:10:57,246 --> 01:11:00,525
...or cut with a sword. How do we defeat it?"

824
01:11:01,406 --> 01:11:03,645
What did I say, my son?

825
01:11:04,406 --> 01:11:06,005
Huh, my Orhan?

826
01:11:08,806 --> 01:11:10,205
Mother..

827
01:11:14,326 --> 01:11:19,245
"When anger blinds one of you...

828
01:11:19,366 --> 01:11:24,685
...the other should be his eyes
so that in the end, you both win.

829
01:11:25,926 --> 01:11:28,285
Don't let anger defeat you.

830
01:11:30,326 --> 01:11:34,205
Never part your ways as brothers.

831
01:11:35,206 --> 01:11:37,445
That's what I said, right?

832
01:11:38,766 --> 01:11:40,445
Do you remember?

833
01:11:50,966 --> 01:11:56,925
Why did you forget it when you
needed to remember the most, my son?

834
01:11:56,926 --> 01:11:58,565
Huh, my Orhan?

835
01:11:59,806 --> 01:12:03,005
He would be your eyes,
and you would be his eyes.

836
01:12:03,006 --> 01:12:05,005
Why did you become blind?

837
01:12:05,366 --> 01:12:08,245
I didn't want it to be like this either, mother.

838
01:12:09,606 --> 01:12:11,565
But Alaeddin..

839
01:12:15,006 --> 01:12:17,685
Alaeddin left me no choice.

840
01:12:17,686 --> 01:12:19,725
So you had no choice but to hit him...

841
01:12:21,646 --> 01:12:25,085
...and he had no choice but to leave, right?

842
01:12:28,726 --> 01:12:30,165
What a shame...

843
01:12:34,406 --> 01:12:38,765
What a shame that I
couldn't teach you anything.

844
01:12:56,126 --> 01:13:00,325
The Kayi tribe is shaken by
Alaeddin's decision to leave.

845
01:13:01,806 --> 01:13:04,525
These are Osman's good days, Vural.

846
01:13:15,126 --> 01:13:16,965
Do you hear that?

847
01:13:19,006 --> 01:13:21,845
Do you hear the sound of the doomsday?

848
01:13:22,406 --> 01:13:24,365
It is coming for Osman.

849
01:13:24,366 --> 01:13:26,805
What is your plan, Begum Hatun?

850
01:13:28,966 --> 01:13:32,605
-When will Alaeddin set out?
-Tomorrow morning.

851
01:13:33,166 --> 01:13:34,685
Good.

852
01:13:35,046 --> 01:13:41,845
Let's throw this precious spark
into Kucar's hands and grow the fire.

853
01:13:55,766 --> 01:13:57,165
Sofia.

854
01:14:05,206 --> 01:14:07,365
What did you do?

855
01:14:07,886 --> 01:14:10,525
Why did you attack the people?

856
01:14:10,686 --> 01:14:15,325
I did what I thought was right.

857
01:14:18,486 --> 01:14:22,085
The only harmless Turk is a
dead Turk. Why should they live?

858
01:14:24,366 --> 01:14:32,245
I was even ready to sacrifice Poena to
make an alliance with Osman, but you...

859
01:14:32,526 --> 01:14:36,925
I told you I didn't come here to
make an alliance with Osman.

860
01:14:36,926 --> 01:14:39,445
I won't sit at the same table with Osman.

861
01:14:39,446 --> 01:14:44,085
I don't want an eternal alliance with Osman!

862
01:14:44,086 --> 01:14:51,365
When the time comes, we will kill him and
take our lands back. But now, for Bursa...

863
01:14:53,046 --> 01:14:54,485
Enough!

864
01:14:56,206 --> 01:14:58,525
You are talking just like a Turk.

865
01:14:58,846 --> 01:15:02,005
Same words. Same thoughts.

866
01:15:02,286 --> 01:15:04,605
It's like Osman is in front of me.

867
01:15:04,806 --> 01:15:07,365
Sofia, understand this.

868
01:15:07,446 --> 01:15:10,205
He thinks the same as you.

869
01:15:10,286 --> 01:15:14,605
After he gets his daughter
back, they will draw their swords!

870
01:15:14,606 --> 01:15:17,845
This alliance will bring
us death. Understand this!

871
01:15:17,846 --> 01:15:22,645
We have no choice but to try, Claudius.

872
01:15:22,886 --> 01:15:25,245
Otherwise, we will lose Bursa.

873
01:15:25,246 --> 01:15:28,765
There is a solution. But this is not it!

874
01:15:28,766 --> 01:15:34,405
Enough Claudius! Don't ruin my plans!

875
01:15:35,566 --> 01:15:37,765
Get out of my way

876
01:15:40,966 --> 01:15:42,045
Calm down.

877
01:15:43,486 --> 01:15:47,045
Calm down. Calm down.

878
01:15:52,526 --> 01:15:54,725
Now tell me.

879
01:15:55,966 --> 01:15:59,605
How did Poena react to the alliance with Osman?

880
01:16:00,686 --> 01:16:05,165
She doesn't know what to
do. She's stuck in the middle.

881
01:16:05,526 --> 01:16:07,925
But she will do what I want.

882
01:16:07,926 --> 01:16:09,525
You see?

883
01:16:09,646 --> 01:16:13,125
No one is eager to make an alliance with Osman.

884
01:16:15,606 --> 01:16:19,445
Now it's my turn. My move.

885
01:16:19,446 --> 01:16:21,285
I invited Osman to the outpost.

886
01:16:24,286 --> 01:16:29,245
I'll kill him there and
disgrace him at the frontiers.

887
01:16:29,846 --> 01:16:31,765
There is no alliance.

888
01:16:33,686 --> 01:16:38,485
I will never let you do that, Claudius.

889
01:16:38,966 --> 01:16:42,325
I am sorry. I really am.

890
01:16:44,446 --> 01:16:47,365
But unfortunately, you don't
have the power to do so.

891
01:16:47,886 --> 01:16:50,285
No matter what comes between him and I...

892
01:16:50,806 --> 01:16:56,285
...even your green eyes, even your red hair...

893
01:16:59,206 --> 01:17:01,405
...you won't be able to stop me.

894
01:17:19,486 --> 01:17:25,085
My Alaeddin, how can we leave like
this without saying goodbye to anyone?

895
01:17:25,086 --> 01:17:27,165
My mother will get even more upset.

896
01:17:28,526 --> 01:17:31,445
Leaving in the morning will
be even harder, my Gonca.

897
01:17:31,766 --> 01:17:36,725
It's better to leave in silence
now. Come on, my rose.

898
01:17:48,006 --> 01:17:51,445
Are you going to leave without
saying goodbye to me, brother?

899
01:17:52,126 --> 01:17:53,285
My Fatma..

900
01:18:00,966 --> 01:18:03,765
My angel...

901
01:18:12,286 --> 01:18:14,045
What are you doing here, Fatma?

902
01:18:14,166 --> 01:18:15,565
Why didn't you sleep?

903
01:18:17,086 --> 01:18:19,845
How can I sleep tonight?

904
01:18:20,446 --> 01:18:22,725
I knew you would leave quietly.

905
01:18:25,246 --> 01:18:26,685
I waited for you.

906
01:18:29,566 --> 01:18:32,285
-You can't go like this, brother.
-Fatma.

907
01:18:33,766 --> 01:18:35,045
My angel.

908
01:18:36,726 --> 01:18:38,805
I don't want to upset anyone.

909
01:18:39,326 --> 01:18:41,845
Why are you doing this, brother?

910
01:18:43,126 --> 01:18:44,005
Why?

911
01:18:45,006 --> 01:18:47,245
We have more sorrow to deal with now.

912
01:18:48,246 --> 01:18:51,285
Brother, don't go. Please don't.
-Fatma.

913
01:18:52,046 --> 01:18:53,805
My pretty sister.

914
01:18:53,806 --> 01:18:55,285
My precious sister.

915
01:18:56,366 --> 01:18:58,045
I'm not going to foreign land.

916
01:18:58,646 --> 01:19:01,285
I'm going to see our grandfather.

917
01:19:03,366 --> 01:19:04,885
I promise you.

918
01:19:05,166 --> 01:19:06,405
I will be back.

919
01:19:06,646 --> 01:19:08,205
I will be back.
-Well...

920
01:19:09,006 --> 01:19:11,125
Who knows when?

921
01:19:11,446 --> 01:19:13,525
We will be far away from each other.

922
01:19:14,286 --> 01:19:15,565
I will miss you.

923
01:19:17,206 --> 01:19:19,365
We will miss you too.

924
01:19:19,886 --> 01:19:21,885
We will miss you too.

925
01:19:26,526 --> 01:19:27,805
A little patience.

926
01:19:28,646 --> 01:19:30,205
Look at me.

927
01:19:33,286 --> 01:19:35,765
Take care of mother and father, alright?

928
01:19:36,766 --> 01:19:38,405
Look after them.

929
01:19:40,326 --> 01:19:41,605
Sister.

930
01:19:42,686 --> 01:19:44,925
Take care of my brother.

931
01:19:53,206 --> 01:19:55,365
Don't worry, my bead-eyed.

932
01:19:57,966 --> 01:19:59,925
I will take a great care of him.

933
01:20:01,126 --> 01:20:02,925
Just don't be sorry.

934
01:20:03,606 --> 01:20:06,565
But keep praying for us, alright?

935
01:20:11,326 --> 01:20:12,445
Fatma.

936
01:20:16,406 --> 01:20:18,405
My angel.

937
01:20:19,046 --> 01:20:21,205
My precious.

938
01:20:21,446 --> 01:20:23,245
Take care of yourself, alright?

939
01:20:23,846 --> 01:20:25,485
Don't upset your brother.

940
01:20:32,806 --> 01:20:34,445
Let's go, my dear. Come on.

941
01:20:34,926 --> 01:20:36,405
Come on.

942
01:20:42,006 --> 01:20:43,765
Here we go.

943
01:20:59,846 --> 01:21:01,325
Father.

944
01:21:06,366 --> 01:21:08,005
Hold this, sister.

945
01:21:51,806 --> 01:21:54,005
May Allah protect you, father.

946
01:22:00,366 --> 01:22:02,805
May Allah always help you.

947
01:22:31,166 --> 01:22:33,965
Let's go, my dear. Come on!

948
01:22:34,526 --> 01:22:36,125
Come on.

949
01:22:41,966 --> 01:22:44,205
Have a safe journey, brother.

950
01:25:32,606 --> 01:25:34,285
Messenger Kucar.

951
01:25:35,086 --> 01:25:37,445
Orlok Kucar.

952
01:25:37,686 --> 01:25:39,085
Orlok.

953
01:25:41,126 --> 01:25:43,525
I was waiting for you, hatun.

954
01:25:44,606 --> 01:25:46,605
Have a seat.

955
01:25:56,566 --> 01:25:58,685
How did you know I would come?

956
01:26:00,246 --> 01:26:03,125
Are they still following me?

957
01:26:04,326 --> 01:26:08,485
Do you know what orlok means, hatun?

958
01:26:09,966 --> 01:26:11,925
It means eagle.

959
01:26:13,486 --> 01:26:17,205
The eagle is in the frontiers now.

960
01:26:17,366 --> 01:26:21,285
And it is watching all of us.

961
01:26:23,846 --> 01:26:26,205
Now tell me.

962
01:26:27,046 --> 01:26:30,045
-Did you consider my offer?
-Your offer...

963
01:26:31,406 --> 01:26:33,085
...is accepted.

964
01:26:33,446 --> 01:26:35,045
Good.

965
01:26:36,766 --> 01:26:39,285
I'll collaborate with you against Osman.

966
01:26:40,886 --> 01:26:43,005
Sharpen your claws now.

967
01:26:44,606 --> 01:26:47,165
I've got important news for you.

968
01:26:48,486 --> 01:26:50,565
Shahzade Alaaddin...

969
01:26:51,286 --> 01:26:53,565
...separated his way from his father's.

970
01:26:54,046 --> 01:26:55,725
He abandoned the tribe.

971
01:26:56,286 --> 01:26:59,205
I've heard that he's going to the light.

972
01:27:01,086 --> 01:27:04,565
It is very important news, hatun.

973
01:27:06,606 --> 01:27:08,565
Good.

974
01:27:10,006 --> 01:27:13,605
One of Osman's children is in my clutches now.

975
01:27:15,046 --> 01:27:18,125
Bring him to me immediately.

976
01:27:26,166 --> 01:27:30,365
When you send his children to Olcaytu,

977
01:27:31,246 --> 01:27:33,605
...will you spare Osman's life?

978
01:27:35,166 --> 01:27:36,725
It's the price...

979
01:27:37,686 --> 01:27:40,245
..of the khan's children.

980
01:27:41,326 --> 01:27:43,965
Fight in the frontiers is inevitable.

981
01:27:44,366 --> 01:27:49,725
Bursa and Kayi will be
the properties of Ilkhanids.

982
01:28:14,646 --> 01:28:19,245
Your hands touch it but your heart is far away.

983
01:28:20,406 --> 01:28:26,565
This silence of yours is
the greatest cry inside me.

984
01:28:26,846 --> 01:28:29,045
I'm hearing your silent cry.

985
01:28:29,366 --> 01:28:31,565
I see the fire in you, Bala.

986
01:28:33,006 --> 01:28:34,605
You don't see, Osman.

987
01:28:35,926 --> 01:28:38,125
You don't see the fire inside me.

988
01:28:38,846 --> 01:28:40,285
My tongue is mute.

989
01:28:40,406 --> 01:28:44,165
But my heart is lamenting.

990
01:28:45,046 --> 01:28:47,565
I have neither a son beside me...

991
01:28:48,166 --> 01:28:50,005
...nor words to say.

992
01:28:50,766 --> 01:28:52,125
No.

993
01:28:52,846 --> 01:28:54,405
Don't look at me like that.

994
01:28:55,206 --> 01:28:56,325
It hurts me.

995
01:28:57,646 --> 01:28:59,565
You think I'm going to the battle.

996
01:29:00,486 --> 01:29:03,805
In fact, the hardest battle for me...

997
01:29:04,846 --> 01:29:06,645
...is your eyes.

998
01:29:07,886 --> 01:29:10,725
I'm right in the middle of the battle.

999
01:29:11,446 --> 01:29:13,205
I can neither come back...

1000
01:29:13,846 --> 01:29:15,325
..nor go ahead.

1001
01:29:17,966 --> 01:29:22,805
Even if your tongue is mute,
you talk with everything else.

1002
01:29:24,286 --> 01:29:28,005
Your eyebrows and eyes are falling on me.

1003
01:29:30,806 --> 01:29:33,285
I can read your mind, Bala.

1004
01:29:34,406 --> 01:29:41,925
But today, what you say in
silence becomes a dagger...

1005
01:29:43,526 --> 01:29:45,245
...and hurts my heart.

1006
01:29:51,166 --> 01:29:53,285
Do I have permission my Bey father?

1007
01:29:58,166 --> 01:29:59,565
Come in, daughter.

1008
01:30:05,246 --> 01:30:06,485
Daughter.

1009
01:30:07,886 --> 01:30:09,885
Is Alaaddin leaving?

1010
01:30:10,886 --> 01:30:11,645
Mother.

1011
01:30:17,726 --> 01:30:19,245
My brother...

1012
01:30:20,166 --> 01:30:21,525
...left last night.

1013
01:30:48,086 --> 01:30:51,045
Your father left quietly and
you didn't tell me, Fatma?

1014
01:30:51,566 --> 01:30:52,565
Mother!

1015
01:30:54,286 --> 01:30:55,525
Bring my horse!

1016
01:30:55,646 --> 01:30:57,165
Kismet, prepare to ride.

1017
01:30:57,326 --> 01:30:59,085
We'll catch up with Alaaddin.

1018
01:31:10,166 --> 01:31:11,445
Not now.

1019
01:31:12,086 --> 01:31:13,365
She's too angry.

1020
01:31:44,046 --> 01:31:45,365
Alps!

1021
01:31:46,406 --> 01:31:48,325
What's wrong with you?

1022
01:31:49,646 --> 01:31:51,365
We're going to the battle!

1023
01:31:51,966 --> 01:31:53,565
Pull yourselves together!

1024
01:31:53,806 --> 01:31:56,565
Nobody will stand with their heads down!

1025
01:32:15,126 --> 01:32:17,565
My Beys! My alps!

1026
01:32:18,446 --> 01:32:21,525
Today is the day to destroy the devil's nest!

1027
01:32:22,806 --> 01:32:25,765
We're going to avenge our martyrs and ghazis.

1028
01:32:25,886 --> 01:32:27,365
Let's go.

1029
01:33:13,206 --> 01:33:16,485
Don't have a sullen face.

1030
01:33:20,486 --> 01:33:23,565
Since that day, I've been
thinking if there was another way.

1031
01:33:26,886 --> 01:33:28,205
My brother...

1032
01:33:32,126 --> 01:33:33,605
Orhan Bey.

1033
01:33:34,966 --> 01:33:36,805
Was Orhan Bey right?

1034
01:33:41,166 --> 01:33:43,405
There wasn't another way, Gonca.

1035
01:33:45,086 --> 01:33:47,325
While my alps were dying one by one.

1036
01:33:47,726 --> 01:33:49,685
...while they were burning alive

1037
01:33:49,966 --> 01:33:51,645
...if I hadn't drew back there,

1038
01:33:53,366 --> 01:33:55,085
...all of them would have died.

1039
01:33:58,126 --> 01:34:00,765
I wouldn't be able to with this guilt then.

1040
01:34:02,206 --> 01:34:03,965
You did the right thing.

1041
01:34:04,126 --> 01:34:06,445
You shouldn't think anymore.

1042
01:34:07,406 --> 01:34:08,925
This is a war.

1043
01:34:09,286 --> 01:34:12,045
You can win and lose.

1044
01:34:12,846 --> 01:34:16,725
With what you did, you prevented a disaster.

1045
01:34:17,126 --> 01:34:18,885
It wasn't a mistake.

1046
01:34:20,126 --> 01:34:22,045
You did the hardest thing.

1047
01:34:23,086 --> 01:34:24,845
You endured, Alaaddin.

1048
01:34:25,726 --> 01:34:29,805
Today, you taught me what endurance means.

1049
01:34:37,646 --> 01:34:41,605
Alaaddin, why are you removing the traces?

1050
01:34:42,046 --> 01:34:44,085
Who would follow us?

1051
01:34:45,046 --> 01:34:49,085
I learned endurance and
struggling from my mother.

1052
01:34:52,526 --> 01:34:54,965
She will come after us.

1053
01:34:55,926 --> 01:34:57,885
That's why I'm removing the traces.

1054
01:34:59,846 --> 01:35:02,165
-Let's go.
-Alright.

1055
01:35:53,926 --> 01:35:56,765
No! No traces at all.

1056
01:35:57,726 --> 01:36:01,525
He said he'd go to the dervish lodge.
Maybe he's gone somewhere else?

1057
01:36:01,726 --> 01:36:03,805
I couldn't see my son one last time.

1058
01:36:04,366 --> 01:36:07,285
My lady, when things
calm down, he will be back.

1059
01:36:07,286 --> 01:36:08,965
He won't stay there forever.

1060
01:36:08,966 --> 01:36:12,285
What we think won't happen
happens all the time, Kismet.

1061
01:36:12,486 --> 01:36:14,085
Alaaddin has gone.

1062
01:36:14,406 --> 01:36:15,645
I couldn't stop him.

1063
01:36:16,166 --> 01:36:17,885
I won't leave Halime, though.

1064
01:36:18,046 --> 01:36:19,845
What's in your mind, Bala Hatun?

1065
01:36:19,846 --> 01:36:21,805
I don't trust the snake called Sofia.

1066
01:36:21,806 --> 01:36:24,485
I'll go and take my daughter from Bursa.

1067
01:36:24,886 --> 01:36:26,045
We're going to Bursa!

1068
01:36:26,166 --> 01:36:28,005
Let's ride! Come on!

1069
01:37:56,726 --> 01:37:58,165
Who are you?

1070
01:38:01,046 --> 01:38:02,245
Who are you?

1071
01:38:19,766 --> 01:38:20,925
You...

1072
01:38:22,246 --> 01:38:23,605
You are me

1073
01:38:25,566 --> 01:38:27,525
You are Holofira.

1074
01:38:32,126 --> 01:38:33,605
You are me.

1075
01:38:34,566 --> 01:38:35,885
I'm not you.

1076
01:38:37,166 --> 01:38:38,045
You..

1077
01:38:42,646 --> 01:38:44,205
...aren't Holofira.

1078
01:38:49,686 --> 01:38:50,845
Then...

1079
01:38:51,806 --> 01:38:53,285
Who am I?

1080
01:39:00,686 --> 01:39:02,205
You'll find this out here.

1081
01:40:15,086 --> 01:40:16,285
Osman.

1082
01:40:17,926 --> 01:40:19,485
I was waiting for you.

1083
01:40:21,766 --> 01:40:23,525
Just like your sons did

1084
01:40:24,966 --> 01:40:28,885
...you will either run away or die.

1085
01:40:30,926 --> 01:40:32,365
It's up to you.

1086
01:40:33,086 --> 01:40:35,005
If you were clever.

1087
01:40:35,606 --> 01:40:37,885
...you would have let my sons kill you.

1088
01:40:40,646 --> 01:40:42,165
Soldiers!

1089
01:41:01,446 --> 01:41:02,725
Well..

1090
01:41:03,566 --> 01:41:06,365
Do you think I don't have a hidden punch?

1091
01:41:08,926 --> 01:41:10,325
Beys!

1092
01:41:11,006 --> 01:41:15,565
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1093
01:41:15,966 --> 01:41:20,445
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1094
01:41:23,166 --> 01:41:26,925
Nice. An easy victory can't be a real victory.

1095
01:41:27,726 --> 01:41:30,285
Soldiers, attack!

1096
01:41:30,326 --> 01:41:31,805
Attack!

1097
01:41:40,646 --> 01:41:43,805
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1098
01:41:59,286 --> 01:42:00,645
Alaaddin.

1099
01:42:04,006 --> 01:42:06,045
Allah..

1100
01:42:09,246 --> 01:42:10,845
Alaaddin.

1101
01:42:11,726 --> 01:42:14,005
I felt happy that you are smiling.

1102
01:42:15,126 --> 01:42:18,205
But right then your smiles
get covered with sorrow.

1103
01:42:18,606 --> 01:42:20,285
I'm fine, my dear.

1104
01:42:24,046 --> 01:42:25,965
It's like, in my heart.

1105
01:42:27,446 --> 01:42:29,325
...I'm carrying what I left behind.

1106
01:42:31,286 --> 01:42:33,845
I can't forget them when I go away.

1107
01:42:35,606 --> 01:42:36,965
I know.

1108
01:42:39,726 --> 01:42:42,325
You're thinking about your father, huh?

1109
01:42:43,886 --> 01:42:45,285
Yes. Yes.

1110
01:42:56,286 --> 01:42:58,565
I disappointed him.

1111
01:43:03,366 --> 01:43:04,805
You say so?

1112
01:43:09,926 --> 01:43:13,605
Great Scholar Alaaddin Ali Bey...

1113
01:43:14,646 --> 01:43:17,925
...has become like a student
who has left home recently, huh?

1114
01:43:18,726 --> 01:43:21,203
What? Should we go back?
If you go back, I will do.

1115
01:43:21,215 --> 01:43:22,045
Hey.

1116
01:43:26,046 --> 01:43:28,885
This is the first day of our new life.

1117
01:43:30,646 --> 01:43:32,765
There is no going back.

1118
01:43:35,006 --> 01:43:36,325
Alright then.

1119
01:43:37,166 --> 01:43:39,325
If we're on the way, we have to go.

1120
01:43:42,766 --> 01:43:44,485
Trickster Hatun.

1121
01:43:46,846 --> 01:43:49,085
With a single word of mine.

1122
01:43:50,086 --> 01:43:52,845
...you start an indefinite journey.

1123
01:43:53,846 --> 01:43:55,885
Aren't you angry with me at all?

1124
01:43:56,846 --> 01:44:02,365
Alaaddin... Even if this way leads to a cliff...

1125
01:44:03,886 --> 01:44:06,085
...or embers...

1126
01:44:07,766 --> 01:44:10,005
...I will still walk with you.

1127
01:44:11,046 --> 01:44:12,565
You say so?

1128
01:44:18,206 --> 01:44:19,485
It means...

1129
01:44:21,926 --> 01:44:24,365
You love me so much, huh?

1130
01:44:25,086 --> 01:44:29,645
Alaaddin... Daisy...

1131
01:44:36,726 --> 01:44:40,405
You want a race again?

1132
01:44:41,046 --> 01:44:42,565
Fine.

1133
01:44:43,446 --> 01:44:47,205
Let's have a race and I will
give you a hard lesson. Scholar.

1134
01:44:47,486 --> 01:44:49,005
-You say so?
-Yes.

1135
01:44:49,326 --> 01:44:50,685
Let's do it.

1136
01:44:51,006 --> 01:44:53,205
So be it. Trickster Hatun.

1137
01:44:54,886 --> 01:44:58,445
-I will show you how to ride.
-You never can.

1138
01:44:59,166 --> 01:45:01,045
Let's see who rides faster.

1139
01:46:11,606 --> 01:46:13,245
Koca Bey!

1140
01:46:13,246 --> 01:46:19,045
It would be a shame for us not to kill
all of them for the innocents we lost.

1141
01:46:55,486 --> 01:46:57,725
Come, Claudius.

1142
01:46:57,726 --> 01:47:00,485
Now it's time to take revenge for our martyrs.

1143
01:47:00,486 --> 01:47:02,685
Come.

1144
01:47:07,566 --> 01:47:10,685
Orhan! Leave that dog to me.

1145
01:47:27,086 --> 01:47:28,685
Osman.

1146
01:47:31,406 --> 01:47:33,645
Stop!

1147
01:47:40,286 --> 01:47:41,725
Sofia.

1148
01:47:46,486 --> 01:47:52,325
By the order of the great
Emperor, I end this war.

1149
01:47:58,366 --> 01:48:01,485
Soldiers! Lower your swords!

1150
01:48:01,486 --> 01:48:03,725
Sofia, are you crazy?

1151
01:48:03,726 --> 01:48:07,325
Soldier! I am commanding you! Attack!

1152
01:48:07,326 --> 01:48:08,805
Stop!

1153
01:48:09,646 --> 01:48:11,205
I said stop!

1154
01:48:17,566 --> 01:48:19,765
What does the Emperor want?

1155
01:48:19,766 --> 01:48:25,365
He wants us to make an alliance
against the Mongols just like I do.

1156
01:48:26,606 --> 01:48:29,605
And in return...

1157
01:48:31,086 --> 01:48:33,525
...the outpost will be yours.

1158
01:48:36,246 --> 01:48:38,805
And during this time

1159
01:48:40,606 --> 01:48:43,925
...Claudius will be under your command.

1160
01:48:45,686 --> 01:48:49,645
Sofia, you must be crazy.

1161
01:48:49,646 --> 01:48:55,805
If you don't obey the order,
you will be punished with death.

1162
01:48:56,126 --> 01:48:57,685
Never!

1163
01:48:58,006 --> 01:49:00,965
I will never side with a Turk.

1164
01:49:00,966 --> 01:49:02,605
Never!

1165
01:49:02,766 --> 01:49:07,725
Infidel leader, we haven't
given up on taking your life either.

1166
01:49:17,766 --> 01:49:21,565
Soldiers, we are retreating.

1167
01:49:40,126 --> 01:49:42,845
Won't we go after them, my Bey?

1168
01:49:45,046 --> 01:49:47,085
Of course, we will.

1169
01:49:47,086 --> 01:49:50,205
I want them, dead or alive. Go.

1170
01:49:50,566 --> 01:49:52,405
Go, Koca Bey.

1171
01:50:04,246 --> 01:50:06,485
So, it's the Emperor's order.

1172
01:50:06,766 --> 01:50:09,885
If there is a game behind this...

1173
01:50:10,006 --> 01:50:13,205
The game is over, Osman Bey.

1174
01:50:13,686 --> 01:50:18,165
Now it's time for unity for Kayi and Bursa.

1175
01:50:20,086 --> 01:50:25,245
Hand over the outpost to Osman Bey.

1176
01:50:40,126 --> 01:50:42,685
So that you want peace...

1177
01:50:43,846 --> 01:50:46,645
...then you will do as I say.

1178
01:50:47,966 --> 01:50:49,765
My daughter Halime...

1179
01:50:49,766 --> 01:50:51,885
You will tell me where she is.

1180
01:50:51,886 --> 01:50:54,085
You will take me to her.

1181
01:50:56,086 --> 01:50:58,245
-Aykurt!
-My Bey.

1182
01:50:58,246 --> 01:51:02,045
Strengthen this outpost.
-As you order, my Bey.

1183
01:51:10,126 --> 01:51:12,445
If you tell me it's the Emperor's order...

1184
01:51:13,126 --> 01:51:15,805
...but play a game...

1185
01:51:16,886 --> 01:51:22,005
...I will slit your throat, not Mongols.

1186
01:51:25,046 --> 01:51:27,965
Alps! Come on!

1187
01:51:40,886 --> 01:51:43,445
You've slowed down. Scholar, huh?

1188
01:51:44,086 --> 01:51:47,285
Good, you must have learned.

1189
01:51:47,286 --> 01:51:49,885
Do you even leave a man
any mind to learn, woman?

1190
01:51:49,886 --> 01:51:51,965
I don't understand, Alaeddin.

1191
01:51:52,446 --> 01:51:58,005
I mean, when I'm with you, I lose my mind.

1192
01:51:58,166 --> 01:52:01,445
No, you can't make me forget
your defeat with these words.

1193
01:52:01,446 --> 01:52:03,565
I'll never forget it, Alaeddin.

1194
01:52:03,566 --> 01:52:06,125
Good, enjoy it for now.

1195
01:52:06,126 --> 01:52:08,565
You'll see if I'll lose to you again.

1196
01:52:08,566 --> 01:52:11,485
-So you lost on purpose, huh? 
-Of course I did.

1197
01:52:18,606 --> 01:52:20,885
Someone's following us.

1198
01:52:20,886 --> 01:52:22,885
What? Who?

1199
01:52:23,406 --> 01:52:24,925
I don't know.

1200
01:52:25,446 --> 01:52:28,605
But they must've been
after us since we left the tribe.

1201
01:52:28,806 --> 01:52:31,005
I don't know what's waiting for us.

1202
01:52:31,686 --> 01:52:34,365
First, we'll find a way to get over them.

1203
01:52:34,526 --> 01:52:37,525
Come after me. Come on.

1204
01:52:37,526 --> 01:52:39,765
Let's go!

1205
01:52:57,606 --> 01:53:02,805
With our alliance, the Mongols will
face the curse of God, Osman Bey.

1206
01:53:03,286 --> 01:53:07,485
Mongols cannot be cursed, Hatun.

1207
01:53:13,126 --> 01:53:20,885
Anyone who sees the shine of their sword
knows that Mongols are the curse itself.

1208
01:53:25,246 --> 01:53:30,005
Everyone who once felt the Mongol
chains on their neck knows that...

1209
01:53:30,006 --> 01:53:34,965
...the mark left by Mongols
does not fade easily.

1210
01:53:36,286 --> 01:53:38,765
After the messenger whose hand I cut off...

1211
01:53:39,646 --> 01:53:43,165
...for trying to touch my
lands, are you saying this?

1212
01:53:44,166 --> 01:53:50,005
The Mongols that make the world unbearable
for you every time you cut off a hand.

1213
01:53:50,006 --> 01:53:57,125
The Mongols that rained their furor
on you every time you went too far.

1214
01:54:01,046 --> 01:54:08,605
From your alliance, I see that
Byzantium also seeks this dark fate.

1215
01:54:09,686 --> 01:54:13,565
Now listen to me carefully.

1216
01:54:14,286 --> 01:54:20,205
With this unity, with this alliance
my messengership ends here.

1217
01:54:20,286 --> 01:54:25,525
Orlok Kucar stands against you from now on.

1218
01:54:30,766 --> 01:54:36,805
Two little sparrows declared war on an eagle.

1219
01:54:38,086 --> 01:54:41,325
Pity. Such a pity.

1220
01:54:42,566 --> 01:54:46,365
The day you said you would annex Bursa...

1221
01:54:47,486 --> 01:54:50,165
...you started that war.

1222
01:54:55,686 --> 01:54:57,965
Two little sparrows, huh?

1223
01:55:01,646 --> 01:55:06,525
Two little sparrows.

1224
01:55:09,886 --> 01:55:12,525
Don't forget the birds of Ababil.

1225
01:55:13,646 --> 01:55:18,285
The Ababil birds that
brought down the elephants...

1226
01:55:21,006 --> 01:55:25,965
...also know how to cut the eagle's claws off.

1227
01:55:30,366 --> 01:55:33,045
If you want war, then let's fight!

1228
01:55:33,046 --> 01:55:34,285
Face me!

1229
01:55:35,646 --> 01:55:36,685
What a pity...

1230
01:55:36,966 --> 01:55:42,925
You chose to perish when you
could have been prisoners but alive.

1231
01:56:14,166 --> 01:56:16,805
Someone is coming. Get off.

1232
01:56:18,286 --> 01:56:20,925
Hide, come on.

1233
01:56:47,886 --> 01:56:49,765
Isn't that Meryem?

1234
01:56:49,766 --> 01:56:52,485
Meryem?

1235
01:56:52,886 --> 01:56:55,405
What is she doing with the soldiers?

1236
01:57:00,166 --> 01:57:03,085
Why is she wearing Byzantium clothes?

1237
01:57:10,526 --> 01:57:12,645
She is running away! Catch her!

1238
01:57:14,486 --> 01:57:17,165
Bala Hatun, what is
happening? I don't understand.

1239
01:57:17,166 --> 01:57:18,765
We'll learn.

1240
01:57:18,766 --> 01:57:20,045
Come on.

1241
01:57:22,086 --> 01:57:26,005
He does not deny that he came
to the frontiers for the annexation.

1242
01:57:26,006 --> 01:57:28,925
He says we started this war.

1243
01:57:28,926 --> 01:57:32,925
We did not start this war, but
we will end it, my Shahzade.

1244
01:57:32,926 --> 01:57:34,005
For sure.

1245
01:57:34,006 --> 01:57:35,845
I told you..

1246
01:57:35,846 --> 01:57:42,325
A decision other than the alliance would
mean welcoming the barbarian Mongol invasion.

1247
01:57:42,606 --> 01:57:49,125
Whoever threatens our state and nation
will certainly face the furor they deserve.

1248
01:57:56,406 --> 01:57:59,405
Why are you in a hurry,
soldier? What is happening?

1249
01:57:59,406 --> 01:58:00,845
Ma'am, Poena.

1250
01:58:00,846 --> 01:58:02,325
She ran away.

1251
01:58:03,646 --> 01:58:05,325
Poena.

1252
01:58:07,766 --> 01:58:08,925
Where did she go?

1253
01:58:08,926 --> 01:58:13,685
She is going south, ma'am.
-Let's go!

1254
01:58:19,406 --> 01:58:22,325
Are you playing games again?

1255
01:58:22,326 --> 01:58:24,405
What kind of a game is this?

1256
01:58:24,406 --> 01:58:27,245
Come on!

1257
01:58:42,646 --> 01:58:44,805
What will I tell them when I see them?

1258
01:58:46,206 --> 01:58:47,525
Meryem

1259
01:58:52,246 --> 01:58:53,765
Bala Hatun.

1260
01:58:53,766 --> 01:58:57,325
My daughter. You are alive, thanks to Allah.

1261
01:58:57,326 --> 01:58:58,365
Are you alright?

1262
01:58:58,366 --> 01:59:00,245
Did they hurt you?

1263
01:59:00,246 --> 01:59:01,725
Do not approach, Bala Hatun.

1264
01:59:01,806 --> 01:59:05,205
Meryem. Meryem stop. They
didn't do something bad to you, right?

1265
01:59:05,206 --> 01:59:07,005
I said stay away, Bala Hatun!

1266
01:59:07,006 --> 01:59:09,085
Come here! What are you doing?

1267
01:59:09,166 --> 01:59:10,685
Meryem, stop.

1268
01:59:12,956 --> 01:59:13,925
Stop.

1269
01:59:13,926 --> 01:59:15,685
I said stay away, Bala Hatun.

1270
01:59:15,686 --> 01:59:17,645
Stay away.

1271
01:59:17,646 --> 01:59:19,845
What are you doing here, my daughter?

1272
01:59:26,686 --> 01:59:28,525
Meryem what is happening?

1273
01:59:28,846 --> 01:59:32,565
I wronged you.

1274
01:59:32,566 --> 01:59:37,525
What do you mean?

1275
01:59:41,526 --> 01:59:44,845
Stay away!

1276
01:59:45,366 --> 01:59:48,205
What do you want from this little girl, huh?

1277
01:59:55,206 --> 01:59:56,645
Bala.

1278
01:59:57,206 --> 02:00:01,285
Osman.

1279
02:00:10,806 --> 02:00:12,445
Meryem.

1280
02:00:17,806 --> 02:00:19,645
What happened?

1281
02:00:19,846 --> 02:00:20,585
I...

1282
02:00:25,726 --> 02:00:28,765
...betrayed my family.

1283
02:00:29,086 --> 02:00:31,525
I betrayed you.

1284
02:00:36,646 --> 02:00:38,045
Poena.

1285
02:01:02,206 --> 02:01:03,805
Come here.

1286
02:01:06,766 --> 02:01:08,405
Halime.

1287
02:01:32,726 --> 02:01:35,005
You are Halime.

1288
02:01:41,966 --> 02:01:44,205
Halime?

1289
02:01:55,686 --> 02:01:59,325
My daughter...

1290
02:01:59,326 --> 02:02:00,805
Sister..

1291
02:02:05,806 --> 02:02:06,995
Osman.

1292
02:02:08,246 --> 02:02:09,485
My daughter...

1293
02:02:45,406 --> 02:02:47,245
Come here Poena.

1294
02:02:47,566 --> 02:02:49,015
Stay away.

1295
02:02:51,286 --> 02:02:53,005
Stay away!

1296
02:02:53,006 --> 02:02:54,965
Stop, my daughter. Alright.

1297
02:02:54,966 --> 02:02:57,005
No one will come close.
Stop.

1298
02:02:57,606 --> 02:02:59,645
No one approach her!

1299
02:03:06,166 --> 02:03:07,845
It's over, my daughter.

1300
02:03:07,886 --> 02:03:09,765
The nightmare is over.

1301
02:03:10,966 --> 02:03:12,405
Come.

1302
02:03:12,406 --> 02:03:14,485
Come, let's reunite...

1303
02:03:15,926 --> 02:03:17,765
I'd love to...

1304
02:03:18,646 --> 02:03:20,325
I'd love to...

1305
02:03:21,526 --> 02:03:23,285
But I cannot come.

1306
02:03:26,926 --> 02:03:29,165
I made many mistakes.

1307
02:03:33,846 --> 02:03:36,725
I don't have the strength to look at your face.

1308
02:03:39,006 --> 02:03:40,125
No.

1309
02:03:40,126 --> 02:03:42,605
No, look. It was not your mistake.

1310
02:03:42,606 --> 02:03:44,085
It was my mistake.

1311
02:03:44,086 --> 02:03:46,845
I couldn't recognize my own child.

1312
02:03:47,406 --> 02:03:52,045
I couldn't recognize my own daughter.

1313
02:03:52,286 --> 02:03:54,365
Forgive me, my child.

1314
02:03:54,686 --> 02:03:56,285
Forgive me.

1315
02:03:57,446 --> 02:03:59,605
Come on. Come. Let's reunite now...

1316
02:03:59,606 --> 02:04:00,805
Come to your mother.

1317
02:04:00,806 --> 02:04:02,285
Come on!

1318
02:04:05,846 --> 02:04:07,325
My daughter...

1319
02:04:08,166 --> 02:04:10,085
Come on, the light of my eye...

1320
02:04:10,086 --> 02:04:11,565
My Halime...

1321
02:04:18,006 --> 02:04:19,725
I can't.

1322
02:04:20,446 --> 02:04:21,965
I can't.

1323
02:04:26,086 --> 02:04:31,765
I can't, I shot you with an arrow...

1324
02:04:34,166 --> 02:04:36,365
How could someone ever shoot her own father?

1325
02:04:40,806 --> 02:04:43,285
Would she ever try to kill her mother?

1326
02:04:46,206 --> 02:04:47,725
I thought...

1327
02:04:48,206 --> 02:04:50,685
...you were my enemies for years.

1328
02:04:52,766 --> 02:04:54,805
This cannot be forgiven.

1329
02:04:56,046 --> 02:04:57,605
No.

1330
02:04:59,286 --> 02:05:01,845
-It's not possible. 
-No.

1331
02:05:01,846 --> 02:05:03,965
Don't even say that.

1332
02:05:04,046 --> 02:05:05,645
Look...

1333
02:05:07,246 --> 02:05:09,565
Children make mistakes.

1334
02:05:10,606 --> 02:05:12,805
Fathers forgive....

1335
02:05:13,966 --> 02:05:16,165
Fathers always forgive them.

1336
02:05:17,006 --> 02:05:18,205
Huh?

1337
02:05:18,846 --> 02:05:20,285
My daughter...

1338
02:05:22,366 --> 02:05:23,725
Come on.

1339
02:05:26,566 --> 02:05:28,365
Come on, give me your hand.

1340
02:05:32,006 --> 02:05:33,745
Come on.

1341
02:05:40,166 --> 02:05:42,365
Poena, don't do something stupid!

1342
02:05:42,886 --> 02:05:44,325
You did nothing wrong!

1343
02:05:44,326 --> 02:05:46,205
It was all my fault!

1344
02:05:49,726 --> 02:05:53,285
You did this! You did this!

1345
02:05:54,136 --> 02:05:59,045
You buried me in your own darkness!

1346
02:06:00,446 --> 02:06:02,565
You shut up!

1347
02:06:02,926 --> 02:06:04,925
Shut up, you snake!

1348
02:06:06,006 --> 02:06:07,405
Sister...

1349
02:06:07,406 --> 02:06:09,125
My sister.

1350
02:06:09,486 --> 02:06:11,365
Come, don't do this.

1351
02:06:12,446 --> 02:06:14,005
Don't make my mother..

1352
02:06:14,246 --> 02:06:15,965
..my father..

1353
02:06:16,646 --> 02:06:19,485
...don't make us suffer from this pain again.

1354
02:06:20,086 --> 02:06:21,725
Come.

1355
02:06:27,926 --> 02:06:29,405
My daughter...

1356
02:06:30,246 --> 02:06:31,925
My Halime...

1357
02:06:33,006 --> 02:06:35,005
It is not your fault.

1358
02:06:35,006 --> 02:06:39,885
You are the most innocent, the
purest among us, my daughter.

1359
02:06:39,886 --> 02:06:42,005
Don't do this to yourself.

1360
02:06:42,006 --> 02:06:44,045
Don't do this to us, come here.

1361
02:06:44,366 --> 02:06:46,245
Come to your mother.

1362
02:06:48,966 --> 02:06:50,445
Halime..

1363
02:06:53,246 --> 02:06:54,805
Meryem.

1364
02:06:59,726 --> 02:07:01,365
Poena.

1365
02:07:04,446 --> 02:07:06,165
Who am I?

1366
02:07:07,086 --> 02:07:08,435
I don't know.

1367
02:07:16,766 --> 02:07:18,405
I don't know.

1368
02:07:19,566 --> 02:07:21,245
What will happen now?

1369
02:07:23,566 --> 02:07:25,805
I lost my memories...

1370
02:07:26,486 --> 02:07:29,565
I lost my childhood!

1371
02:07:33,686 --> 02:07:35,005
My past...

1372
02:07:37,366 --> 02:07:38,965
...is filled with lies!

1373
02:07:38,966 --> 02:07:40,725
Forget about the past!

1374
02:07:40,726 --> 02:07:42,565
It's over now!

1375
02:07:45,366 --> 02:07:46,925
Look at me..

1376
02:07:48,046 --> 02:07:49,565
But now..

1377
02:07:49,566 --> 02:07:51,605
We have future.

1378
02:07:52,206 --> 02:07:54,485
We have a future together.

1379
02:07:55,286 --> 02:07:56,485
Halime.

1380
02:07:57,086 --> 02:07:58,165
My daughter.

1381
02:07:58,846 --> 02:08:00,325
Look at me.

1382
02:08:01,726 --> 02:08:03,645
There are five steps between us.

1383
02:08:05,286 --> 02:08:07,365
Do you know what five steps are?

1384
02:08:09,126 --> 02:08:11,285
This is our feast.

1385
02:08:12,246 --> 02:08:14,045
Today is the reunion day

1386
02:08:14,646 --> 02:08:15,645
My dear.

1387
02:08:16,326 --> 02:08:17,405
Come.

1388
02:08:17,886 --> 02:08:19,565
Come here, my baby gazelle.

1389
02:08:20,566 --> 02:08:21,805
Come.

1390
02:08:22,926 --> 02:08:24,885
Do you remember...

1391
02:08:25,766 --> 02:08:28,365
...what I told you in the cave?

1392
02:08:29,966 --> 02:08:33,045
What we did with that shadow play?

1393
02:08:33,606 --> 02:08:36,725
The wolf and the baby gazelle?

1394
02:08:39,966 --> 02:08:41,325
Do you remember?

1395
02:08:44,126 --> 02:08:45,645
I tired really hard.

1396
02:08:47,606 --> 02:08:49,005
But I couldn't.

1397
02:08:52,966 --> 02:08:54,725
I went to that cave...

1398
02:08:57,606 --> 02:09:00,285
...to kill you, father.

1399
02:09:05,526 --> 02:09:07,045
But it didn't happen.

1400
02:09:07,326 --> 02:09:08,645
It didn't happen.

1401
02:09:09,326 --> 02:09:13,285
Your heart didn't let your mind.

1402
02:09:20,326 --> 02:09:22,085
I don't know who I am.

1403
02:09:22,206 --> 02:09:23,645
Whoever you are.

1404
02:09:23,806 --> 02:09:29,645
Meryem or Poena or Halime

1405
02:09:30,606 --> 02:09:32,405
...you are who you are.

1406
02:09:33,326 --> 02:09:35,165
You are our daughter.

1407
02:09:35,526 --> 02:09:36,965
You are.

1408
02:09:37,126 --> 02:09:38,325
Right, Bala?

1409
02:09:39,126 --> 02:09:41,285
Yes. Yes.

1410
02:09:42,366 --> 02:09:43,805
We want you.

1411
02:09:44,086 --> 02:09:45,325
Just you.

1412
02:09:45,686 --> 02:09:47,325
I want to hug you.

1413
02:09:47,526 --> 02:09:50,645
I want to caress your hair,
my dear. Come to your mother.

1414
02:09:51,286 --> 02:09:52,325
Come.

1415
02:09:52,566 --> 02:09:55,925
You can kill me but don't do this. Come on.

1416
02:10:00,966 --> 02:10:02,365
Come here. Poena.

1417
02:10:03,526 --> 02:10:07,045
Look at me. I called you Halime.

1418
02:10:07,886 --> 02:10:10,325
I named you after my mother.

1419
02:10:11,566 --> 02:10:13,565
I never saw my mother.

1420
02:10:15,206 --> 02:10:17,485
But I wanted her to live with you.

1421
02:10:19,926 --> 02:10:22,165
I wanted her name to live in you.

1422
02:10:22,606 --> 02:10:24,205
My Halime.

1423
02:10:26,366 --> 02:10:28,045
My daughter...

1424
02:10:32,486 --> 02:10:33,765
Don't.

1425
02:10:34,486 --> 02:10:36,725
Don't. Look at me.

1426
02:10:37,006 --> 02:10:38,645
The past is over.

1427
02:10:39,926 --> 02:10:41,645
We have a future now.

1428
02:10:43,606 --> 02:10:45,005
Give me your hand.

1429
02:10:49,806 --> 02:10:50,965
Come on.

1430
02:11:14,886 --> 02:11:17,485
Sofia stabbed me in the back.

1431
02:11:23,646 --> 02:11:25,005
Are you surprised?

1432
02:11:26,646 --> 02:11:29,925
You once said she could do anything.

1433
02:11:30,206 --> 02:11:32,165
I expected anything but...

1434
02:11:32,926 --> 02:11:36,085
I never expected Sofia...

1435
02:11:39,046 --> 02:11:44,485
...to have an alliance with Osman
and go convince the emperor.

1436
02:11:46,446 --> 02:11:47,485
Demon.

1437
02:11:57,566 --> 02:12:01,565
One is demon. The other one is improvident.

1438
02:12:04,246 --> 02:12:10,765
Osman's killing Olcaytu's
daughter and grandson...

1439
02:12:11,686 --> 02:12:14,965
...opened the gates of Bursa for us.

1440
02:12:19,646 --> 02:12:22,445
Nobody can stop us now.

1441
02:12:23,006 --> 02:12:24,845
Neither Osman...

1442
02:12:25,446 --> 02:12:29,125
...nor your emperor who
believes in their alliance.

1443
02:12:30,246 --> 02:12:32,365
Damn the emperor.

1444
02:12:43,966 --> 02:12:47,085
As Olcaytu promised you,

1445
02:12:48,326 --> 02:12:51,125
..when all the heads falls on the ground.

1446
02:12:51,846 --> 02:12:55,565
...you will ascend the throne in Bursa.

1447
02:12:56,526 --> 02:12:59,205
Under the banner of Ilkhanids,

1448
02:12:59,486 --> 02:13:02,045
...your reign will begin.

1449
02:13:02,446 --> 02:13:07,725
But if we fail to take...

1450
02:13:08,166 --> 02:13:13,645
...what Olcaytu wants as the price of
his daughter and grandson from Osman

1451
02:13:17,566 --> 02:13:20,365
...then our heads will fall on the ground.

1452
02:13:52,326 --> 02:13:53,965
What do you want this time?

1453
02:13:54,126 --> 02:13:55,645
You vile dogs!

1454
02:13:56,606 --> 02:13:58,765
What are you up to this time?

1455
02:14:04,206 --> 02:14:07,045
Gonca, I know them.

1456
02:14:08,046 --> 02:14:11,005
They are hell hounds!
Just go away and save yourself.

1457
02:14:11,286 --> 02:14:13,765
I will leave you alone, Alaaddin.

1458
02:14:14,126 --> 02:14:16,365
Come here, dogs.

1459
02:14:17,606 --> 02:14:21,165
Come here, come here.

1460
02:14:26,966 --> 02:14:28,645
Gonca, be careful.

1461
02:14:42,486 --> 02:14:44,645
-Gonca?
-Alaaddin.

1462
02:14:45,166 --> 02:14:46,645
Don't be afraid.

1463
02:14:47,606 --> 02:14:49,445
You vile dogs.

1464
02:14:50,766 --> 02:14:52,285
-Come on.
-Come on!

1465
02:15:00,486 --> 02:15:02,205
Gonca. Gonca.

1466
02:15:02,926 --> 02:15:04,645
-Don't touch her!
-Alaaddin!

1467
02:15:04,766 --> 02:15:07,085
-Leave her! Don't touch her!
-Get off!

1468
02:15:07,246 --> 02:15:08,645
Leave her!

1469
02:15:09,686 --> 02:15:11,045
Alaaddin!

1470
02:15:22,726 --> 02:15:24,925
How long I looked for you!

1471
02:15:25,366 --> 02:15:27,405
How badly my heart hurt!

1472
02:15:27,846 --> 02:15:29,645
You saw it for yourself.

1473
02:15:29,846 --> 02:15:31,565
Now I've found you.

1474
02:15:32,646 --> 02:15:33,965
Don't do this, my dear.

1475
02:15:46,246 --> 02:15:48,685
You can kill me but don't do this.

1476
02:15:49,006 --> 02:15:50,645
I'm begging you. Come here.

1477
02:15:50,886 --> 02:15:52,445
Come hug me.

1478
02:16:00,766 --> 02:16:02,725
Come on, Halime. Come on, my dear.

1479
02:16:03,046 --> 02:16:05,165
Halime, hold our hands.

1480
02:16:05,406 --> 02:16:08,125
Halime, after you hold my hand

1481
02:16:08,126 --> 02:16:12,045
...we won't have sorrow but happiness.

1482
02:16:12,246 --> 02:16:13,925
Come on.

1483
02:16:22,966 --> 02:16:26,045
Come on, my dear. Hold my hand.

1484
02:16:31,246 --> 02:16:33,565
-Father.
-My daughter.

1485
02:16:48,686 --> 02:16:51,205
-Mother.
-My dear.

1486
02:17:00,486 --> 02:17:01,924
Forgive me.

1487
02:17:02,126 --> 02:17:04,325
Halime. Halime!

1488
02:17:11,085 --> 02:17:12,165
Poena.

1489
02:17:12,486 --> 02:17:14,125
-My dear.
-Forgive me.

1490
02:17:14,126 --> 02:17:16,245
-Don't Halime..
-No!

1491
02:17:16,286 --> 02:17:17,885
Halime!

1492
02:17:20,846 --> 02:17:23,805
-Sister! Halime!
-My daughter!

1493
02:17:24,165 --> 02:17:27,485
-Halime!
-My daughter!

1494
02:17:28,846 --> 02:17:30,565
Halime!

1495
02:17:31,046 --> 02:17:33,165
My baby!

1496
02:17:33,886 --> 02:17:36,205
Halime!

1497
02:17:38,886 --> 02:17:40,445
Sister!

1498
02:17:45,206 --> 02:17:47,045
My baby...